COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[220,"§Monkey\nMonkey is an animal found mostly in India and Africa. The merchant fleets of Sulaiman(as) which roamed the seas sometimes had monkeys with them. ( See : Bible, Kings, 10:22)\nApes and monkeys have been described in three places in the Holy Quran. They have been mentioned in connection with the tribes who disobeyed the commands of Allah(swt) and were thus turned into apes. ( See : Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-65, Surah-5, Al-Ma’ida, Verse-60, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-166)."],[221,"§Month\nEach year has twelve months.\nإِنَّ عِدَّةَ الشُّهُورِ عِندَ اللَّهِ اثْنَا عَشَرَ شَهْرًا فِي كِتَابِ اللَّهِ يَوْمَ خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ مِنْهَا أَرْبَعَةٌ حُرُمٌ\nIndeed, the number of months with Allah is twelve [lunar] months in the register of Allah [from] the day He created the heavens and the earth; of these, four are sacred.\n[At-Tawba: 36]\nHere by ‘register’ is meant the ‘Lauhe-Mahfooz’ in which each and everything about this entire creation has been written down. The Arabs, the Jews and the Hindus have all divided a year into twelve months based on the rotation and revolution of the moon. The Arabic months are as follows:\n1.Muharram 2. Safar 3. Rabi al-Awwal 4.Rabi ath-Thani 5.Jumada al-Ula 6.Jumada al-Akhira 7.Rajab 8. Shaban 9. Ramadan 10. Shawwal 11.Dhu al-Qada 12.Dhu al-Hijja.\nOf these four are sacred. They are : Dhu al-Qada, Dhu al-Hijja, Muharram and Rajab. It was forbidden to fight wars in these months. But the ignorant ancient tribes started changing these months so that the problem of ‘not fighting in the forbidden months’ could be circumvented. This has been described as ‘Nasi’ in the Holy Quran. ‘Nasi’ means to change the months.( See Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-37). Due to this changing of the months according to their convenience, there was deviation in the months as ordained by Allah(swt). It is one of the miracles of the Holy Prophet(saws) that just a few years after his prophethood the months came back to their original state, that is the months which were ‘haram’ became as such and this state shall remain till the Last Day. Since ancient times some tribes based their calendar on the sun. These are as follows in the Syriac and Latin calendars:\nS.No.SyriacLatinS.No.SyriacLatin\n1CanunJanuary7TamuzJuly\n2ShubatFebruary8AbAugust\n3AdarMarch9ElulSeptember\n4NisanApril10Tishri priorOctober\n5IyarMay11Tishri posteriorNovember\n6ChaziranJune12Canun priorDecember\nFor example:\n‘Nisan’ (Nehemiah 2:1)\n‘Elul’ (Nehemiah 6:15)\n‘Adar’ (Esther 3:7)\n‘Shubat’ (Zechariah 1:7)\nIn a few Arab countries like Syria, Lebanon, Iraq, Yemen etc, even today these Syriac names are used. They are not aware of the Latin names.\nThe twelve lunar months add up to 354 days and the twelve solar months add up to 365. So, the Jews increased one month every three years so as to make it on par with the solar calendar. Some scholars have termed this also as ‘Nasi’ because this also led to a change in the months as ordained by Allah(swt) and as a result the exact date of festivals etc. could not be ascertained.\nSo, all things in Islam like the fasts of Ramadan, Hajj, festivals (Id) etc are based on the lunar calendar. Only the timings of the five everyday salahs are based on the sun."],[222,"§Moon\nThree words have been used in Arabic for ‘moon’. One is ‘hilal’ when it just appears and looks like a dried up date branch. Second is ‘badr’ when on the fourteenth day it is a bright circle. Third is ‘qamar’ while referring to it on the remaining days. The word used in the Holy Quran is ‘Qamar’. Moon is a bright and beautiful sphere of light traversing the sky. Since ancient times people have attributed various stories to it. Before the advent of Islam, people were worshipping the moon and had included it among their various gods and goddesses. Islam condemns all these superstitions and blind beliefs and explains that Allah(swt) has created the sun and moon and that they are moving in their respective orbits for a time specified by Him(swt).\nاللَّهُ الَّذِي رَفَعَ السَّمَاوَاتِ بِغَيْرِ عَمَدٍ تَرَوْنَهَا ۖ ثُمَّ اسْتَوَىٰ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ ۖ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ ۖ كُلٌّ يَجْرِي لِأَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى ۚ يُدَبِّرُ الْأَمْرَ يُفَصِّلُ الْآيَاتِ لَعَلَّكُم بِلِقَاءِ رَبِّكُمْ تُوقِنُونَ\nIt is Allah who erected the heavens without pillars that you [can] see; then He established Himself above the Throne and made subject the sun and the moon, each running [its course] for a specified term. He arranges [each] matter; He details the signs that you may, of the meeting with your Lord, be certain.\n[Ar-Ra’d: 2]\nIn fact they are for the service of man as the Holy Quran says:\nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ دَائِبَيْنِ ۖ وَسَخَّرَ لَكُمُ اللَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ\nAnd He subjected for you the sun and the moon, continuous [in orbit], and subjected for you the night and the day.\n[Ibraheem: 33]\nThe above verse says that the sun and the moon are not gods but are the obedient slaves created by Allah(swt) and are in fact serving man. They are the servants of man and not the other way round. So we should neither prostrate to the sun nor to the moon but to Allah(swt) who has created them.\nوَمِنْ آيَاتِهِ اللَّيْلُ وَالنَّهَارُ وَالشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ ۚ لَا تَسْجُدُوا لِلشَّمْسِ وَلَا لِلْقَمَرِ وَاسْجُدُوا لِلَّهِ الَّذِي خَلَقَهُنَّ إِن كُنتُمْ إِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُونَ\nAnd of His signs are the night and day and the sun and moon. Do not prostrate to the sun or to the moon, but prostrate to Allah, who created them, if it should be Him that you worship.\n[Fussilat: 37]\n﴿وَآيَةٌ لَّهُمُ اللَّيْلُ نَسْلَخُ مِنْهُ النَّهَارَ فَإِذَا هُم مُّظْلِمُونَ ٣٧ وَالشَّمْسُ تَجْرِي لِمُسْتَقَرٍّ لَّهَا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ تَقْدِيرُ الْعَزِيزِ الْعَلِيمِ ٣٨ وَالْقَمَرَ قَدَّرْنَاهُ مَنَازِلَ حَتَّىٰ عَادَ كَالْعُرْجُونِ الْقَدِيمِ ٣٩ لَا الشَّمْسُ يَنبَغِي لَهَا أَن تُدْرِكَ الْقَمَرَ وَلَا اللَّيْلُ سَابِقُ النَّهَارِ ۚ وَكُلٌّ فِي فَلَكٍ يَسْبَحُونَ ٤٠﴾\nAnd a sign for them is the night. We remove from it [the light of] day, so they are [left] in darkness. And the sun runs [on course] toward its stopping point. That is the determination of the Exalted in Might, the Knowing. And the moon - We have determined for it phases, until it returns [appearing] like the old date stalk. It is not allowable for the sun to reach the moon, nor does the night overtake the day, but each, in an orbit, is swimming.\n[Ya-sin: 37-40]\nيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْأَهِلَّةِ ۖ قُلْ هِيَ مَوَاقِيتُ لِلنَّاسِ وَالْحَجِّ ۗ وَلَيْسَ الْبِرُّ بِأَن تَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِن ظُهُورِهَا وَلَٰكِنَّ الْبِرَّ مَنِ اتَّقَىٰ ۗ وَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ أَبْوَابِهَا ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ\nThey ask you, [O Muhammad], about the new moons. Say, \"They are measurements of time for the people and for Hajj.\" And it is not righteousness to enter houses from the back, but righteousness is [in] one who fears Allah. And enter houses from their doors. And fear Allah that you may succeed.\n[Al-Baqara: 189]\nThe Holy Quran also has a surah by this name called ‘Suratul-Qamar’. It has 55 verses and the first verse goes as:\nThe Hour has come near, and the moon has split [in two].\nThe reference is to a particular miracle. When the people of Mecca asked the Holy Prophet(saws) to perform a miracle, he(saws) pointed to the moon which split into two. ( See Bukhari, 3636-3638 and Muslim, 2800, 2803)\nThis is confirmed from the records of ancient history also. When the king of Malabar saw the moon split into two he set out to meet the Holy Prophet(saws) but he died before reaching Madina."],[223,"§Mosquito\nMosquito is a very insignificant creature. Its comparison is given in a derogatory sense. It is mentioned in the Bible that Isa(as) said about the Pharisees:\n“O blind guides! You strain out a mosquito but swallow the camel.”\n(Matthew, 23:24)\nIts example is mentioned in the Holy Quran only once:\nإِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يَسْتَحْيِي أَن يَضْرِبَ مَثَلًا مَّا بَعُوضَةً فَمَا فَوْقَهَا\nIndeed, Allah is not timid to present an example - that of a mosquito or what is smaller than it.\n[Al-Baqara: 26]\nThe disbelievers of Islam rejected the Holy Quran saying that if it is indeed the word of Allah(swt), then why are the lowly creatures like mosquitoes and flies mentioned in it?\nAllah(swt) says that for the purpose of explanation Allah(swt) does not shy from giving the example of an insignificant creature like the mosquito. The ultimate aim is to make the message clear and for this purpose if the example of a mosquito needs to be used then there should be no cause for hesitation.\nActually the disbelievers of Islam wanted to reject the Holy Quran and stop people from believing in it and so they started using this sort of silly and lame excuses."],[224,"§Moth\nMoth is an insect which hovers near a lamp. This has been mentioned in the Holy Quran only once to describe the condition of the people on Doomsday; the people will be running hither and thither like moths dispersed on that day as they will not be able to find any refuge:\nيَوْمَ يَكُونُ النَّاسُ كَالْفَرَاشِ الْمَبْثُوثِ\nIt is the Day when people will be like moths, dispersed.\n[Al-Qari’a: 4]"],[225,"§Mu’akhah\nThe meaning of ‘Mu’akhah’ is to make someone a brother. This is a golden example in the history of Islam which cannot be compared to anything else in the entire human history. The explanation is as follows. When the Holy Prophet(saws) migrated from Makka to Madina following the command of Allah(swt), other Muslims also started migrating to Madina to safeguard their religion as the atrocities of the disbelievers had become unbearable. These immigrants (Muhajir) left behind everything – their homes, businesses, wealth and sometimes their families too. Now the main problem which arose was the question of settling these Muhajirs. So, the people of Madina who were called Ansar (helpers) and the Muhajirs were bound by ‘Mu’akhah’. That is, when a Muhajir came from Makkah, the Holy Prophet(saws) called an Ansar and made both of them brothers. The Ansar would whole-heartedly accept the Muhajir as his brother and be ready to make him the owner of half his property. So much so that if somebody had two wives, he would say to the Muhajir, “I shall divorce whoever pleases you and after the waiting period (iddat) you may marry her.”\nThis was what transpired between Sad-bin-Rabi’a Ansari and Abdur-Rehman-bin-Ouf Muhajir. Sad-bin-Rabi’a told Abdur-Rehman-bin-Ouf, “Whatever wealth I have we shall share equally. I have two wives and of them I shall divorce whoever pleases you and after she becomes legal you may marry her.”\nAbdur-Rehman-bin-Ouf replied, “May Allah(swt) increase your wealth and family. Just show me the way to the market.”\nIn this way he went to the market and started his own business. Allah(swt) made him successful in it and he also married a woman from Madina. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 3781)\nIn this way the Holy Prophet(saws) established Mu’akhah between ninety people (45 Muhajir and 45 Ansar). Some scholars are of the opinion that the Holy Prophet(saws) established Mu’akhah between the people of Makka before the Hijrat (migration). But no mention of any such thing is found in books before third century A.H. So, Shaiqul-Islam and Ibn-Taimiyah have refuted this.\nThis Mu’akhah was practiced for some time till the Muhajirs could stand on their own feet. Then in Surah-8, An-Anfal which was revealed after the war of Badr, the laws of inheritance between the Muhajirs and Ansar brothers as a result of ‘Mu’akhah’ were nullified:\nوَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مِن بَعْدُ وَهَاجَرُوا وَجَاهَدُوا مَعَكُمْ فَأُولَٰئِكَ مِنكُمْ ۚ وَأُولُو الْأَرْحَامِ بَعْضُهُمْ أَوْلَىٰ بِبَعْضٍ فِي كِتَابِ اللَّهِ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمٌ\nAnd those who believed after [the initial emigration] and emigrated and fought with you - they are of you. But those of [blood] relationship are more entitled [to inheritance] in the decree of Allah. Indeed, Allah is Knowing of all things.\n[Al-Anfal: 75]"],[226,"§Muhaarba\nSee ‘Struggle’."],[227,"§Muhammad(saws)\nBefore the advent of Islam, people with many faiths existed in Arabia. They could be broadly divided into two groups. The first group were the ‘atheists’ who denied the existence of Allah(swt) or any other god. They did not believe that there is life after death. They simply believed in living this life merrily eating, drinking and having fun. They said that once they die that was the end and that they would not be raised up again nor would they have to answer for their deeds in this world.\nThe second group were the religious ones and could further be divided into two. The first of these believed in ‘monotheism’ and were called ‘Hanafiya.’ But these were very few. The second group were the idol-worshippers. They believed that the angels and the spirits of their forefathers possessed psychic powers and that by worshipping these they could please Allah(swt). So, they made idols of these and would bow down to them and seek favours from them. They also firmly believed that these would intercede on their behalf with Allah(swt).\nThe most popular among these idols were Hubal, Wadh, Suwa’a, Yaghoos, Yaookh, Nasar, Uzza, La’at and Manat. In the same way, the idols of Ibraheem(as) and Maryam were also made and were in fact kept inside the Holy Kaaba.\nUnder these conditions the Holy Prophet(saws) was made a prophet and sent to these people so that he(saws) could invite them to the true path and the worship of the one true Allah(swt).\nThe life of Prophet Muhammad(saws) can be divided into two parts:\nFirst part: This spans the time from his birth to the attainment of prophethood at the age of forty.\nSecond part: This spans the time from the attainment of prophethood at the age of forty to his demise.\nThe first part of the life of the Holy Prophet(saws):\nBefore narrating his life history, let us take a look at the existing conditions of Arabia and the city of Makkah. Arabia was from Syria to Yemen and from the Red Sea to the Gulf of Arabia. The people were from the tribe of Ismael-bin-Ibraheem. Hence the Holy Prophet(saws) was from the progeny of Ibraheem(as).\nProphet Muhammad(saws) was born in 12 Rabi Al Awwal, Monday, corresponding to 20 or 22 April 571 A.D in Makkah. His father Abdullah died before his birth. It is narrated in the sahih hadith that after his birth there was such a light that the area till Syria was illuminated. (Hadith: Mustadrak Haakim, 2/600, Musnad Ahmad, 4/127). According to the custom of those days, he(saws) was sent to a nearby village where Halima Sadiya suckled him and he was reared in the fresh air of the country. But one day such a miracle occurred that Halima returned the baby to Aaminah. This is described in the sahih hadith as follows:\n“He(saws) was playing with some friends when Jibrail(as) came, lay him down on the ground, tore open his chest, removed his heart, washed it with zam-zam water which he had brought with him in a golden vessel and then replaced it.”\n(Sahih Muslim, 1/147)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was five years old at the time. The meaning of this miracle is that Allah(swt) cleansed his heart of all evils like shirk etc. and was thus being conditioned for the prophethood which he was to receive in future. He(saws) was not even six when his mother Aaminah passed away. He(saws) became an orphan. But his paternal grand-father Abdul-Mutallib took up the responsibility of bringing him up. Even he passed away when Muhammad(saws) was just eight years old. His paternal uncle Abu-Talib, who was very fond of Muhammad(saws) took up the responsibility next. He took very good care of his nephew. He even took him along on trade and other journeys. Muhammad(saws) also took excellent care of his uncle. It is narrated in Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim that Muhammad(saws) took the goats of the people of Makkah for grazing (Sahih Bukhari, 2262 and Sahih Muslim, 2050). This shows that his uncle was not very well off and therefore Muhammad(saws) helped him out in this way.\nWhen Muhammad(saws) was just twenty-five, he had earned a name among the people of Quraish as a very truthful person and one with excellent character. A rich and noble lady of Quraish, Khadija(ra) married him. Khadija was forty at the time and was already widowed twice. After marriage he(saws) started living in Khadija’s house which was a short distance away from Mount Marwa. He(saws) lived here till his migration.\nFor details about his marriages see ‘Muhammad(saws)s and his wives’.\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) was thirty-five years old, the people of Quraish decided to rebuild the Holy Kaaba. When it was time to put the ‘Hijr-e-Aswad’ in its place, the people started quarrelling as to who should get this honour because every family wanted to do this sacred task. Then the oldest among them suggested that the first person to enter the Kaaba the next day should solve this problem. The next day, Muhammad(saws) was the first person to enter the Kaaba. When the people saw him they exclaimed that this was a very just person. They accepted him as the judge. When this problem was presented to Muhammad(saws), he asked for a piece of cloth to be brought. He(saws) then placed the Hijr-e-Aswad on it and said, “Now all the people lift it with the help of the cloth.” When it was brought to its place, Muhammad(saws) picked it up and placed it in its place. (See: Musnad Ahmad 3/425 and Haakim Mustadrak 3/458). In this way he(saws) prevented a major fight from breaking out. While this incident highlights the wisdom of the Holy Prophet(saws), it also shows how he(saws) was renowned for his just and fair nature even before he attained prophethood.\nWhen he was forty years old he started having dreams which would turn out to be true. In this way it was indicated to him that shortly he would be getting revelations. Whenever possible, he(saws) would retire to Mount Hira and engage in the remembrance of Allah(swt). He would mostly prefer to be alone and contemplate on Allah(swt) and His(swt) Creation in seclusion. When he(saws) saw the people of his tribe engaged in idolatry, he was deeply saddened. He(saws) wanted them to forsake polytheism and idol-worship and start worshipping the one true Allah(swt) who had created them and the entire universe. So, he would often go away to a cave on Mount Hira and spend time worshipping and remembering Allah(swt).\nThe first part of the life of the Holy Prophet(saws):\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) was forty years, on a Monday in the month of Ramadan a miracle took place. The Holy Prophet(saws) was engrossed in the remembrance of Allah(swt) when Jibrail(as) came to him and said,”I am an angel of Allah(swt) and following His(swt) command I come to you with the divine revelation. So read.” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “But I cannot read.” Then Jibrail(as) pulled Muhammad(saws) towards himself with all his strength, embraced him and then released him and said,”Read.” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “I cannot read.” Jibrail(as) again pulled Muhammad(saws) towards himself, embraced him and then released him and said,”Read.” The Holy Prophet(saws) again replied, “I cannot read.” The third time Jibrail(as) said,\n﴿اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ ١ خَلَقَ الْإِنسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ ٢ اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الْأَكْرَمُ ٣ الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ ٤ عَلَّمَ الْإِنسَانَ مَا لَمْ يَعْلَمْ ٥﴾\nRecite in the name of your Lord who created - Created man from a clinging substance. Recite, and your Lord is the most Generous - Who taught by the pen - Taught man that which he knew not.\n[Al-Alaq: 1-5]\nThis was the first revelation. After this the Holy Prophet(saws) went home. His heart was beating wildly. He(saws) told his wife Khadija,” Cover me with a blanket.” When he had calmed down he narrated the whole incident to her and also said, “I fear for my life.” Khadija reassured him saying, “I swear by Him(swt) in whose hand is the soul of Khadija, you will be the messenger of this ummah. You always speak the truth, you keep good relations with your kith and kin, help the poor and destitute, serve your guests generously, and assist the deserving when calamity afflicts them. How will Allah(swt) destroy you?” Then she took him to her paternal cousin Waraka-bin-Nawfal who had embraced Christianity and had read the Christian religious books and was writing the Injeel in Arabic. He was ninety years old at the time. After listening to the entire narration he said, “I swear in the name of God, this is the same angel who had come to Musa(as). I am convinced that Allah(swt) has made you a prophet. I wish I would be alive to see the day when your people will become your enemies and drive you out of this place.” The Holy Prophet(saws) asked, “Will they drive me out?” Waraqa replied in the affirmative and said, \"Anyone (man) who came with something similar to what you have brought was treated with hostility; and if I should remain alive till the day when you will be turned out then I would support you strongly.\" But after a few days Waraqa died.\nAfter this there was no further revelation for six months and the Holy Prophet(saws) was very sad. This was actually a test for the Holy Prophet(saws) so that he(saws) could differentiate between the revelations from Allah(swt) and the whisperings and thoughts which the Satan put in his heart. Then after six months there came the revelation which was:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ ١ قُمْ فَأَنذِرْ ٢ وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ ٣ وَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ ٤ وَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْ ٥ وَلَا تَمْنُن تَسْتَكْثِرُ ٦ وَلِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْ ٧﴾\nO you who covers himself [with a garment], Arise and warn .And your Lord glorify .And your clothing purify .And uncleanliness avoid .And do not confer favor to acquire more .But for your Lord be patient.\n[Al-Muddathir: 1-7]\nThe uncleanliness can be that of either shirk or physical dirt. (See Sahih Bukhari, 8/678 and Sahih Muslim, 1/143)\nNow the gigantic task of guiding humanity towards the straight and true path was placed on his shoulders. This is the beginning of his prophethood. This is made up of two phases – the Makkan phase which began when he(saws) was forty years old to his migration to Madina when he(saws) was fifty-three and the Madina phase which started from his migration when he was fifty-three to his demise at the age of sixty-three; that is ten years.\nThe Makkan phase:\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) began preaching Islam, the first person to embrace Islam was his wife Khadija(ra) who helped him heart and soul. Then Ali(ra), son of his paternal uncle Abu Talib embraced Islam. Ali was just ten years old at that time. Among the older people who entered the fold of Islam was Abu Bakr who was thirty-eight. Among the slaves, Zaid-bin-Haris was the first person to enter the fold of Islam.\nAccording to a sahih hadith S’ad bin Abi Waqqas was the third person to enter the fold of Islam. (Sahih Bukhari: 71, 83, 170)\nFor three years the Holy Prophet(saws) propagated Islam secretly and people started accepting it secretly. After three years Allah(swt) revealed the following verse:\n﴿وَأَنذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ الْأَقْرَبِينَ ٢١٤﴾\nAnd warn, [O Muhammad], your closest kindred.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 214]\nThat is, invite your nearest relatives towards Islam and warn them of the impending punishment. That is, only those who have believed shall enter Paradise while the disbelievers shall be tormented forever in hell-fire.\nAfter this was revealed, the Holy Prophet(saws) climbed a mountain called Safa and called out to the people, “Ya Sahaba!” Hearing this all the people of Quraish assembled there. Then the Holy Prophet(saws) called out to each and every group and said,\n'O people! Will you believe me if I say there is an army marching behind this mountain which is about to attack you?'\nThey all answered, 'Of course we would, we have not heard a lie from you throughout your life'.\nMuhammad, The Last Prophet (saws) said, 'O people of Quraish! I warn you to fear God's punishment. Save yourself from the fire. My position is the same as that of the sentry who sees the enemy from afar and warns his people of the danger of their enemies. Does such a person ever lie to his people?'\nHearing these words many people became very angry and said,”Is this why you have assembled us here?” His paternal uncle, Abu Lahab who was also present there said, “May you perish! Is this why you have called us here?” He was an open enemy of the Holy Prophet(saws) till he died. His wife also tormented the Holy Prophet(saws) by spreading thorns in his path. The surah Al-Lahab was revealed about this couple:\n﴿تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِي لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ ١ مَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُ مَالُهُ وَمَا كَسَبَ ٢ سَيَصْلَىٰ نَارًا ذَاتَ لَهَبٍ ٣ وَامْرَأَتُهُ حَمَّالَةَ الْحَطَبِ ٤ فِي جِيدِهَا حَبْلٌ مِّن مَّسَدٍ ٥﴾\nMay the hands of Abu Lahab be ruined, and ruined is he.His wealth will not avail him or that which he gained.He will [enter to] burn in a Fire of [blazing] flame .And his wife [as well] - the carrier of firewood. Around her neck is a rope of [twisted] fiber.\n[Al-Lahab: 1-5]\nNow the Holy Prophet(saws) openly started calling people towards Islam. On various occasions, he(saws) started preaching to the people that the Creator of this entire universe is the One and only Allah(swt) and therefore He(swt) alone is worthy of worship and worshipping anyone or anything other than Allah(swt) or supplicating to anyone else or bowing down to someone else other than Him(swt) is forbidden or haram. He(saws) also declared that he(saws) was sent as a messenger from Allah(swt) and that success could be attained only by believing in his prophethood.\nOn one hand the Holy Prophet(saws) was inviting the people towards Islam using all his powers while the Quraish on the other hand were violently opposing his message.\nThe Holy Quran kept being revealed and depending on the various situations and problems at various times, different verses were revealed. The miraculous Quran started entering the hearts of the people encouraging them to lay the foundation of a new society. It became the topic of discussion outside Makkah too and people started coming to Makkah in groups. They heard the Holy Quran and started embracing Islam. All the while the people of Quraish started spreading false rumours about the Holy Prophet(saws). Sometimes they called him a poet and sometimes they called him mad. Zimad from Azd Shanoa tribe once came to Makkah and heard that there was a prophet whom the people of Makkah called mad. He could drive away the jinn from the people who were possessed. He told the Holy Prophet(saws),” I can drive away the jinn who has possessed you.” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied,”All praises are for Allah(swt). Him alone do we praise and Him alone do we ask for help. Whom Allah(swt) guides none can lead astray and whom Allah(swt) lets go astray, none can guide to the straight path. I bear witness that none is worthy of worship other than Allah(swt) and Muhammad(saws) is His(swt) slave and messenger.” Zimad said, “Repeat whatever you have said.” In this way he heard the Holy Prophet(saws) thrice. Then Zimad said,”I swear by Allah(swt) that I have heard priests, magicians and poets many times, but I have not heard the words which you utter from anyone else.” Then he embraced Islam.\n(See: Sahih Muslim (2/593)). In the same way Abu-Zar embraced Islam and the narration can be found in Sahih Bukhari (7/173) and Sahih Muslim (4/1923)\nThe Holy Quran was casting its spell far and wide and the disbelievers were doing everything in their power to keep the people away from it. So much so that when their evil plots failed, they started tormenting Muhammad(saws) and his followers in all possible ways.\nOne day the Holy Prophet(saws) was offering salah in the Holy Kaaba. Some disbelievers came there. When he(saws) was in the state of prostration, they heaped the entrails of a camel on him so that he(saws) wasn’t able to get up. When this news reached Fatima, the youngest daughter of the Holy Prophet(saws), she came running and removed the unclean things from his back. Muhammad(saws) was greatly pained by this. After his salah he(saws) cursed the people of Quraish three times and cursed Umr-bin-Hisham, Uthba-bin-Rabia, Waleed-bin-Uthba, Umayya-bin-Khalaf, Uqba-bin-Abi Mu’it and Umara-bin-Waleed that they be destroyed.\nAbdullah-bin-Masood says, “I have seen all these people killed in the battle of Badr. Then their bodies were thrown in a well.”\nIn the same way the Holy Prophet(saws) forbade people from polytheism and idol-worship. He(saws) called people towards monotheism and even warned them that if they did not heed his warning a painful punishment would engulf them.\nThe disbelievers of Makkah tormented Muhammad(saws) and his followers in many ways and the atrocities they inflicted on the people embracing Islam are truly heart-wrenching and horrendous. Some were made to lie down on the burning sands of the desert, sometimes hot boulders were put on their chests and some were drowned in water. Hot iron rods were put in their necks. The slave Bilal was handed over to their children who would put a rope round his neck and drag him along the streets of Makkah like some animal. In spite of all these tortures they did not forsake the true religion. All this pain inflicted on his followers greatly pained the Holy Prophet(saws). Finally he(saws) decided to send away some Muslims to Ethiopia because he(saws) had heard that the king of that place Najashi was a just and good ruler.\nBut the disbelievers of Makkah followed these people to Ethiopia and instigated the king against these Muslims. The king called the refugees to his court and questioned them. He asked them their opinion about Isa(as). The people made Zafar-bin-Abu Talib their representative. He read out the Surah Maryam from the Holy Quran in which it is mentioned that Isa(as) is the slave of Allah(swt). He preached the worship of the One True God Allah(swt). He also refuted that God had taken a son (Inna Aoozubillah). He also gave a brief explanation of the religion of Islam. Hearing all this the king Najashi broke down and his beard became wet with tears. The Christian priest who was seated near him also started weeping. Then Najashi said, “I swear by Allah(swt) that this comes from the same light which was brought by Musa(as). You can stay peacefully in my kingdom and nobody shall harm you here.” It is narrated in a sahih hadith that the king himself secretly accepted Islam and gave testimony to the prophethood of Muhammad(saws).\nWhen the disbelievers could not succeed in bringing back the Muslims from Ethiopia, they started plotting again. They told the Bani-Hashim that if they do not either slay the Holy Prophet(saws) or make him subservient to them, they would face social boycott. This was a very difficult period for the Bani-Hashim but they did not betray the Holy Prophet(saws). His uncle Abu-Talib fled to a valley along with Bani-Hashim. They earned their livelihood there by grazing goats. There was nothing to eat or drink and it is narrated in the sahih hadith that they had to eat the leaves of trees. They were subject to this social boycott for three years. The Holy Quran was being revealed and Allah(swt) commanded them to bear these difficulties with patience. After three years there was dissent among the people of Makkah and they themselves put an end to this boycott. At one time the Holy Prophet(saws) also cursed the people of Makkah due to which there was a terrible drought and the people were even forced to eat dead animals. Abu-Sufyan, who was a prominent chieftain of Makkah and who had not yet embraced Islam came running to the Holy Prophet(saws) and begged him to pray to Allah(swt) to end the drought. As a result of his prayer the drought came to an end and the smoke which was spreading across the skies and scaring the people of Makkah also dispersed. In spite of these miracles the people of Makkah did not turn believers.\nDeath of his uncle Abu-Talib:\nA few days after the end of boycott, his uncle Abu-Talib passed away. He was a source of great strength to the Holy Prophet(saws). It was due to the fear and respect which his uncle commanded that the disbelievers of Makkah dared not harm the Holy Prophet(saws) in any way. But after his death, they became free to torment the Holy Prophet(saws) and his companions without any fear.\nDeath of his wife Khadija:\nA few days after the death of his uncle, his wife Khadija also passed away and it saddened the Holy Prophet(saws) greatly.\nPropagation of Islam outside Makkah:\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) saw that the people of Makkah had hardened their stance towards him and Islam, he(saws) started making plans of propagating Islam outside Makkah. He(saws) went to a nearby place called Ta’if where lived the tribe of Banu-Saqeef. He(saws) preached the message of Islam to them, but they stoned him due to which blood started flowing from his leg. The Holy Prophet(saws) was deeply saddened. So much so that there came a message from Allah(swt) that if the Holy Prophet(saws) wished the people of Makkah and the nearby places would be crushed between the surrounding hills. But there was no feeling of vengeance on the part of the Holy Prophet(saws) and he(saws) prayed to Allah(swt), “O Allah(swt)! Show them the true path.” It is narrated in the Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim that the Holy Prophet(saws) prayed, “O Allah(swt), I am convinced that from among the progeny of these people there will be some who shall worship only You(swt) and will not resort to any form of shirk.” (Sahih Bukhari, 3231 and Sahih Muslim, 1795)\nAfter spending ten days in Ta’if, the Holy Prophet(saws) came back to Makkah. To calm his disturbed mind, Allah(swt) made him travel the seven skies. He(swt) first took him to Baitul-Muqaddas from Makkah and then made him tour the seven skies where the Holy Prophet(saws) saw a great many things.\n(See: Quran, Surah Bani-Israel and Sahih Bukhari, 3207, Sahih Muslim, 164)\nIt was on this journey that the five times salah was made obligatory. He(saws) saw both heaven and hell. The Holy Prophet(saws) was asked, ”Did you see Allah(swt)?” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “He(swt) is a light. How can anybody see Him(swt).” That is, on this journey Allah(swt) showed the Holy Prophet(saws) everything which is hidden from our eyes. This filled his heart with a new strength and he(saws) started propagating Islam with renewed vigour.\nIslam in Madina:\nThe news about Islam had reached Madina by this time. During the time of Hajj, the Holy Prophet(saws) would meet the chieftains of the tribes and give them the message of Islam. This was the tenth year of his prophethood. He(saws) met the pilgrims (Hajis) who had come from Madina in a place called Aqba. He(saws) gave them the message of Islam, hearing which they became Muslims because they had heard from the Jews of Madina that the Last Prophet(saws) was to come. When they heard the Holy Prophet(saws) they were convinced that this was the very prophet whose coming was prophesied by the Jews.\nThe next year during the time of Hajj, the Holy Prophet(saws) gave the message of Islam to the pilgrims. 72 people had come from Madina and all of them became Muslims and promised to give the Holy Prophet(saws) every form of protection and then went back to Madina. There they started propagating Islam and waited for the Holy Prophet(saws) to come to Madina. But the Holy Prophet(saws) was waiting for the command from Allah(swt) to migrate from Makkah to Madina. It is narrated in Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim that the Holy Prophet(saws) dreamt that he(saws) was going from Makkah to a place which was full of date palms. The Holy Prophet(saws) thought that maybe the place was Yamama or Hajar. Then he(saws) saw that the place was Yathrib (another name for Madina). (See Sahih Bukhari 3622 and Sahih Muslim 2272)\nThe disbelievers of Makkah were worried that the followers of the Prophet(saws) outside Makkah would increase and create problems for them. So, they plotted to kill the Holy Prophet(saws). So, all the sub-tribes of Quraish like Bani-Naufal, Bani Abd-Shams, Bani Abdud-Daar, Bani Asad, Bani Makhzoom, Bani-Saham and Bani-Jumh assembled in a place called ‘Daar-Nadwa’. They decided that one person from each clan would be chosen and all these representatives would be given a sword each and then they planned that when the Holy Prophet(saws) came out of his house, they would together slay him. In this way no one clan would be solely responsible for the murder and the Bani-Hashim could not possibly retaliate against all the clans and they would be rid of the Prophet(saws) for good. Later on, they would together pay up the blood-money. Allah(swt) intimated the Holy Prophet(saws) about this evil plot. This is described in Surah-8, Al-Anfal, Verse-30 of the Holy Quran:\nوَإِذْ يَمْكُرُ بِكَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لِيُثْبِتُوكَ أَوْ يَقْتُلُوكَ أَوْ يُخْرِجُوكَ ۚ وَيَمْكُرُونَ وَيَمْكُرُ اللَّهُ ۖ وَاللَّهُ خَيْرُ الْمَاكِرِينَ\nAnd [remember, O Muhammad], when those who disbelieved plotted against you to restrain you or kill you or evict you [from Makkah]. But they plan, and Allah plans. And Allah is the best of planners.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was commanded to migrate from Makkah to Madina. He(saws) summoned Ali(ra) and handed over the various things deposited with him by the people of Makkah with instructions to return them to their respective owners and then follow him to Madina. He(saws) made Ali(ra) lie down in his bed and reciting the surah Yasin, he(saws) came out of his house. When he came to verse-9 of Surah-36, Ya-sin:\nوَجَعَلْنَا مِن بَيْنِ أَيْدِيهِمْ سَدًّا وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ سَدًّا فَأَغْشَيْنَاهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُبْصِرُونَ\nAnd We have put before them a barrier and behind them a barrier and covered them, so they do not see.\nHe(saws) saw that the people who were waiting to kill him were sleeping near the entrance. He(saws) took up a handful of mud and threw it on them as a result of which they could not get up from their sleep. When the Holy Prophet(saws) had left the place, somebody came and informed them that the Prophet(saws) had left. When they barged inside the house they saw that Ali(ra) was sleeping in the Prophet(saws)’s bed. The Holy Prophet(saws) went to Abu-Bakr’s house and both of them left for Madina. This was on 20 June, 622 B.C, Monday. This is the first day of the Islamic calendar.\nWhen the disbelievers of Makkah came to know of the fleeing of the Holy Prophet(saws), they started chasing him. To escape the enemies, the Holy Prophet(saws) and Abu-Bakr hid in a cave on a mountain named Saur. The enemies came to the cave, but when they saw that a spider had weaved a web across the mouth of the cave they went back thinking that nobody could have gone inside without disturbing the web. (See Hadith: Musnad Ahmad 1/348). This was a miracle from Allah(swt) to protect His(swt) slave.\nIn this way both the Holy Prophet(saws) and Abu-Bakr were hidden in the cave for three days. During this time the enemies came till the mouth of the cave. Terrified Abu-Bakr said, “O Prophet of Allah(swt)! If the enemies look into the cave near their feet, they shall see us.” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Abu-Bakr(ra), we are not just two but Allah(swt) is also with us.” (Sahih Bukhari: 3653 and Sahih Muslim 2381)\nVerse-40 of Surah-9, At-Tawba of the Holy Quran also refers to this incident:\nإِلَّا تَنصُرُوهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللَّهُ إِذْ أَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ثَانِيَ اثْنَيْنِ إِذْ هُمَا فِي الْغَارِ إِذْ يَقُولُ لِصَاحِبِهِ لَا تَحْزَنْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ مَعَنَا ۖ فَأَنزَلَ اللَّهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَيْهِ وَأَيَّدَهُ بِجُنُودٍ لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلَىٰ ۗ وَكَلِمَةُ اللَّهِ هِيَ الْعُلْيَا ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ\nIf you do not aid the Prophet - Allah has already aided him when those who disbelieved had driven him out [of Makkah] as one of two, when they were in the cave and he said to his companion, \"Do not grieve; indeed Allah is with us.\" And Allah sent down his tranquillity upon him and supported him with angels you did not see and made the word of those who disbelieved the lowest, while the word of Allah - that is the highest. And Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\nWhen the disbelievers were convinced that the Holy Prophet(saws) and Abu-Bakr(ra) had escaped, they made an announcement that the person who would either kill both of them or capture them alive would be given a reward of one hundred camels. Hearing this a disbeliever Suraqa-bin-Malik set out to capture them. When he reached them the forelegs of his horse sank into the ground and he fell down. He got up and shouted, “I am Suraqa-bin-Malik. I do not wish to harm you as I have come to know that the religion of Muhammad(saws) will definitely spread far and wide.” The Holy Prophet(saws) told Abu-Bakr, “Ask him what he wants?” When Abu-Bakr asked him, he replied, “Give it to me in writing.” The Holy Prophet(saws) asked Abu-Bakr to give it to him in writing. So, he wrote a peace bond taking which he went back. (See Sahih Bukhari 3906)\nThen when the Holy Prophet(saws) was returning from the expedition of Hunain and Ta’if, Suraqa showed him the chit and embraced Islam.\nThe people of Madina came to know that the Holy Prophet(saws) had left Makkah for Madina, so they would wait for him every day outside Madina and when the heat became intense they would go back. Then one day when all the people had gone back to their homes, the Holy Prophet(saws) entered Quba. He camped there for fourteen days. He(saws) built the first mosque of Islam here and this is described in the Holy Quran as well. (See: Quran, Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-108)\nThe Madina phase:\nThirteen years after prophethood, when the Holy Prophet(saws) was fifty-three, he came to Madina. Every person in Madina wanted the Holy Prophet(saws) to stay at his place and he(saws) was in a dilemma as he(saws) did not want to disappoint anybody. So, he(saws) said, “Free my camel and by the command of Allah(swt), wherever she sits, I shall stay there.” (See: Ibn-Hisham 1/495 and Albidaya and Annihaaya 3/200).\nAfter roaming around, the camel stopped near the door-step of Abu-Ayyub. The Holy Prophet(saws) got down and stayed there. There was an open ground there where people dried dates. He(saws) asked, “Whom does this land belong to?” He(saws) was told that it belonged to the two orphaned children of Banu-Najjar. (See: Sahih Bukhari 7/265)\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) bought it and ordered that a mosque be built there and he(saws) along with the Muslims built it. The people of Madina helped the people who came from Makkah whole-heartedly and that is why they were called Ansar which means ‘helpers’.\nThe problem of the people coming from Makkah was solved by the Holy Prophet(saws) in a unique way. He(saws) handed over the immigrants to the people of Madina and told them, “From today both of you are brothers.” The people of Madina were called Ansar (helpers) and the people of Makkah were known as Muhajirs (people who migrate in the way of Allah(swt)). The Ansar very gladly made the Muhajirs their brothers. They took them home and got ready to hand over half their house, wealth and their date orchards. According to historical narrations the Ansar Sad-bin-Rabia had two wives and he told his Muhajir brother, “I shall divorce whoever pleases you and you can marry her after the waiting period.” But the Muhajir Abdur-Rehman invoked blessings on him and said, “Just show me the way to the market.” Then he started his own business as he was a trader. He became prosperous and later on married a lady from Madina.\nWhen the Holy Prophet(saws) saw traces of yellow perfume on the clothes of Abdur-Rehman, he(saws) asked him, “What is this?” Abdur-Rehman replied, “I have married an Ansar lady.” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “In that case you should give a Walima dawat even if it is just one sheep.” (See: Sunan Nasai, 6/137)\nIn this way the Ansar helped the Muhajirs in such an exemplary way that it shall remain a shining light till the Last Day:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ تَبَوَّءُوا الدَّارَ وَالْإِيمَانَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ يُحِبُّونَ مَنْ هَاجَرَ إِلَيْهِمْ وَلَا يَجِدُونَ فِي صُدُورِهِمْ حَاجَةً مِّمَّا أُوتُوا وَيُؤْثِرُونَ عَلَىٰ أَنفُسِهِمْ وَلَوْ كَانَ بِهِمْ خَصَاصَةٌ ۚ وَمَن يُوقَ شُحَّ نَفْسِهِ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ ٩﴾\nAnd [also for] those who were settled in al-Madinah and [adopted] the faith before them. They love those who emigrated to them and find not any want in their breasts of what the emigrants were given but give [them] preference over themselves, even though they are in privation. And whoever is protected from the stinginess of his soul - it is those who will be the successful.\n[Al-Hashr: 9]\nThe Muhajir brothers were not greedy and what they did in return was noble.\nTreaty with the Jews of Madina:\nMadina was inhabited by both the Arabs and the Jews. Islam was spreading fast among the Arabs and it would not be an exaggeration to say that there was not a single house in which at least one person had not become a Muslim.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) feared that the disbelievers of Makkah may instigate the Arabs of other countries against Muhammad(saws) and his followers and that they may wage a war against the Muslims. So, the Holy Prophet(saws) made a treaty with the Jews of Madina. According to this treaty, if somebody attacked Madina, then they would help the Muslims and the growing strength of Islam would not harm them. And in case of an invasion on Madina, the Muslims would safeguard them.\nThe war of Badr:\nBadr is the name of a village about 80 miles south-west of Madina. This is the place where the first war between the Muslims and the disbelievers took place in 2 A.H when the disbelievers attacked Madina to destroy the Muslims. The Muslims emerged victorious in this war. But this made the other Arabs wary of the growing strength of the Muslims.\nThe war of Uhud:\nUhud is the name of a mountain near Madina. This was waged by the disbelievers of Makkah to avenge the killing of their chieftains in the battle of Badr. So, in 3 A.H. the disbelievers of Makkah set out to attack Madina. They had just reached Mount Uhud when the Holy Prophet(saws) and his followers surrounded them. But in this war the Muslims suffered great losses and the Holy Prophet(saws) himself was wounded.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) lived in Madina for ten years. He(saws) had to wage many wars during this period; the prominent ones are: Badr, Uhud, Khandaq, Hudaibiya, Khyber, the victory over Makkah, Hunain and Tabook. In the tenth year of Hijrat, he(saws) performed the Hajj pilgrimage in which one lakh twenty thousand Muslims took part. On 9 Zil Hijja, the Holy Prophet(saws) gave a historic sermon in Arafat in which he gave some very important instructions. A few of them are:\n1. There is no difference between an Arab and a non-Arab; all of us are the children of Adam(as) and Adam(as) was created from mud.\n2. All Muslims are brothers to each other.\n3. Treat your slaves well. Feed them what you eat and clothe them what you wear.\n4. Fear Allah(swt) in the matter of women. They have a right over you and you over them.\n5. I am leaving behind two things. If you firmly hold on to them you shall never go astray. One is the Holy Quran and the other is my sunnah.\nThen addressing the people, the Holy Prophet(saws) asked, “Before Allah(swt) if you are asked about me what shall you say?” The people replied, ‘We shall only say that you have conveyed the message of Allah(swt).’ Then the Holy Prophet(saws) lifted his finger towards the sky and said, “O Allah(swt)! You be the witness.”\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) successfully completed the task assigned to him. The religion brought by him had spread from the Gulf of Arabia to the nearby countries and Allah(swt) also declared that the religion was now complete:\nالْيَوْمَ أَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِينَكُمْ وَأَتْمَمْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ نِعْمَتِي وَرَضِيتُ لَكُمُ الْإِسْلَامَ دِينًا\nThis day I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you and have approved for you Islam as religion.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 3]\nAfter this verse was revealed some people understood that the time had come for the Holy Prophet(saws) to depart from this world and that is what happened. After returning from the Hajj pilgrimage, the Holy Prophet(saws) fell ill and passed away on 12 Rabi’ul Awwal 11 A.H. that is 642 A.D. He(saws) was buried at the same place which is now inside Masjid-e-Nabawi.\nBefore the death of the Holy Prophet(saws) the Holy Quran had been written down and many people had also memorized it. The Holy Quran in its present form is the same as that left behind by the Holy Prophet(saws). Today there are lakhs of Muslims who know the Holy Quran by heart.\nLet us now have a look at what the Holy Quran says about the Holy Prophet(saws):\n1. Allah(swt) sent Muhammad(saws) as His messenger and prophet:\n﴿هُوَ الَّذِي أَرْسَلَ رَسُولَهُ بِالْهُدَىٰ وَدِينِ الْحَقِّ لِيُظْهِرَهُ عَلَى الدِّينِ كُلِّهِ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ ٩﴾\nIt is He who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to manifest it over all religion, although those who associate others with Allah dislike it.\n[As-Saff: 9]\n﴿إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ بِالْحَقِّ بَشِيرًا وَنَذِيرًا ۖ وَلَا تُسْأَلُ عَنْ أَصْحَابِ الْجَحِيمِ ١١٩﴾\nIndeed, We have sent you, [O Muhammad], with the truth as a bringer of good tidings and a warner, and you will not be asked about the companions of Hellfire.\n[Al-Baqara: 119]\n﴿إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَا إِلَيْكُمْ رَسُولًا شَاهِدًا عَلَيْكُمْ كَمَا أَرْسَلْنَا إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ رَسُولًا ١٥﴾\nIndeed, We have sent to you a Messenger as a witness upon you just as We sent to Pharaoh a messenger.\n[Al-Muzammil: 15]\n2. The Holy Prophet(saws) was sent as the last messenger. That is, no other messenger shall come after him. Now, till the last day the only path to success is to believe in the Holy Prophet(saws) and follow his instructions because he(saws) has been sent as the messenger for the entire humanity. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿مَّا كَانَ مُحَمَّدٌ أَبَا أَحَدٍ مِّن رِّجَالِكُمْ وَلَـٰكِن رَّسُولَ اللَّـهِ وَخَاتَمَ النَّبِيِّينَ ۗ وَكَانَ اللَّـهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمًا ٤٠﴾\nMuhammad is not the father of [any] one of your men, but [he is] the Messenger of Allah and last of the prophets. And ever is Allah, of all things, Knowing.\n[Al-Ahzab: 40]\nThe word used in the Holy Quran is ‘Khatam’ which means ‘seal’ and also ‘last’. The Holy Prophet(saws) is the last messenger and after his passing away a seal has been placed on the further arrival of messengers and hence no other prophet shall come. It was declared by the Holy Prophet(saws) that no other prophet shall come after him.\n3. Allah(swt) has praised the excellent character of the Holy Prophet(saws). Before prophethood, he(saws) was known as ‘Amin’ (meaning trustworthy) among his people. After prophethood his character became even better. The Holy Quran says about this:\n﴿ن ۚ وَالْقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ ١ مَا أَنتَ بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ بِمَجْنُونٍ ٢ وَإِنَّ لَكَ لَأَجْرًا غَيْرَ مَمْنُونٍ ٣ وَإِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ ٤ فَسَتُبْصِرُ وَيُبْصِرُونَ ٥ بِأَييِّكُمُ الْمَفْتُونُ ٦﴾\nBy the pen and what they inscribe, You are not, [O Muhammad], by the favor of your Lord, a madman. And indeed, for you is a reward uninterrupted. And indeed, you are of a great moral character. So you will see and they will see .Which of you is the afflicted [by a devil].\n[Al-Qalam: 1-6]\nTaking a pledge at the hand of the Holy Prophet(saws) is equivalent to taking a pledge at the hand of Allah(swt).\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يُبَايِعُونَكَ إِنَّمَا يُبَايِعُونَ اللَّـهَ يَدُ اللَّـهِ فَوْقَ أَيْدِيهِمْ ۚ فَمَن نَّكَثَ فَإِنَّمَا يَنكُثُ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِهِ ۖ وَمَنْ أَوْفَىٰ بِمَا عَاهَدَ عَلَيْهُ اللَّـهَ فَسَيُؤْتِيهِ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا ١٠﴾\nIndeed, those who pledge allegiance to you, [O Muhammad] - they are actually pledging allegiance to Allah. The hand of Allah is over their hands. So he who breaks his word only breaks it to the detriment of himself. And he who fulfills that which he has promised Allah - He will give him a great reward.\n[Al-Fath: 10]\nWhen the Arabs pledged to do something, they would hold each other’s hand and take an oath in the name of Allah(swt). This was called ‘Ba’ith’. Breaking this was considered extremely wrong. It is being explained in the above verse that taking ‘Ba’ith’ at the hand of the Holy Prophet(saws) is like taking ‘Ba’ith’ at the hand of Allah(swt) and hence people should abstain from breaking it. This verse while stressing the importance of ‘Ba’ith’ also highlights the high position accorded to the Holy Prophet(saws).\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) propagated Islam according to the divine revelations:\n﴿وَالنَّجْمِ إِذَا هَوَىٰ ١ مَا ضَلَّ صَاحِبُكُمْ وَمَا غَوَىٰ ٢ وَمَا يَنطِقُ عَنِ الْهَوَىٰ ٣ إِنْ هُوَ إِلَّا وَحْيٌ يُوحَىٰ ٤﴾\nBy the star when it descends, Your companion [Muhammad] has not strayed, nor has he erred, Nor does he speak from [his own] inclination. It is not but a revelation revealed.\n[An-Najm: 1-4]\n﴿قُلْ مَا كُنتُ بِدْعًا مِّنَ الرُّسُلِ وَمَا أَدْرِي مَا يُفْعَلُ بِي وَلَا بِكُمْ ۖ إِنْ أَتَّبِعُ إِلَّا مَا يُوحَىٰ إِلَيَّ وَمَا أَنَا إِلَّا نَذِيرٌ مُّبِينٌ ٩﴾\nSay, \"I am not something original among the messengers, nor do I know what will be done with me or with you. I only follow that which is revealed to me, and I am not but a clear warner.\"\n[Al-Ahqaf: 9]\nقُلْ أَيُّ شَيْءٍ أَكْبَرُ شَهَادَةً ۖ قُلِ اللَّهُ ۖ شَهِيدٌ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَكُمْ ۚ وَأُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنُ لِأُنذِرَكُم بِهِ وَمَن بَلَغَ\nSay, \"What thing is greatest in testimony?\" Say, \"Allah is witness between me and you. And this Qur'an was revealed to me that I may warn you thereby and whomever it reaches.\n[Al-An’am: 19]\nقُلْ إِنَّمَا أَنَا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ يُوحَىٰ إِلَيَّ أَنَّمَا إِلَٰهُكُمْ إِلَٰهٌ وَاحِدٌ\nSay, \"I am only a man like you, to whom has been revealed that your god is one God.\n[Al-Kahf: 110]\nAllah(swt) sent the Holy Prophet(saws) as a messenger for the entire humanity:\n﴿مَا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ إِلَّا كَافَّةً لِّلنَّاسِ بَشِيرًا وَنَذِيرًا وَلَـٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ٢٨﴾\nAnd We have not sent you except comprehensively to mankind as a bringer of good tidings and a warner. But most of the people do not know.\n[Saba: 28]\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) explained this as follows:\n“Before me prophets were sent for their specific tribes but I have been sent for the entire humanity.” (Sahih Bukhari, 335)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“I have been sent for the entire humanity and the chain of prophets ends with me.” (Sahih Muslim, 523)\nThat is why after becoming a Muslim there should not be any feeling of distinction on the basis of colour, caste, creed, wealth or nationality. There is no place for any such difference in an Islamic society. Any Muslim can marry another Muslim according to the rules of Islam, can pray in any mosque along with the other Muslims and can become a scholar of Quran. That is, ordinarily there is no distinction whatsoever in all Islamic matters and if there does exist a distinction, then it is against the principles of Islam.\n7. Miracles related to the Holy Prophet(saws): Many miracles were performed by the Holy Prophet(saws) which are described in the sahih hadith. For example the splitting of the moon (See: Sahih Bukhari, 4864 and Sahih Muslim, 2800), water flowing out of the fingers of the Holy Prophet(saws) (See: Sahih Bukhari, 3579), the food of two-three people being sufficient for a thousand people in the war of Khandaq (See: Sahih Bukhari, 4101). Saib-bin-Yazid who was afflicted with some disease was brought to the Holy Prophet(saws) by his maternal aunt. The Holy Prophet(saws) prayed to Allah(swt) and cured him and he lived to a ripe old age of ninety-four and never fell ill till he died. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 190 and Sahih Muslim, 2345). In this way many miracles are described in the sahih hadith. But the most miraculous thing which shall remain till the Last Day is the noble Quran. As described earlier when Jibrail(as) came with the Holy Quran in the cave of Hira and commanded the Holy\nProphet(saws), “Read”, the Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “I cannot read.” It has been corroborated by the Holy Quran also that the Holy Prophet(saws) could neither read nor write:\n﴿قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّـهِ إِلَيْكُمْ جَمِيعًا الَّذِي لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۖ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ ۖ فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّـهِ وَرَسُولِهِ النَّبِيِّ الْأُمِّيِّ الَّذِي يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّـهِ وَكَلِمَاتِهِ وَاتَّبِعُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ ١٥٨﴾\nSay, [O Muhammad], \"O mankind, indeed I am the Messenger of Allah to you all, [from Him] to whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. There is no deity except Him; He gives life and causes death.\" So believe in Allah and His Messenger, the unlettered prophet, who believes in Allah and His words, and follow him that you may be guided.\n[Al-A’raf: 158]\nOne meaning of ‘ummi’ is unlettered, that is someone who cannot read or write. The society in which the Holy Prophet(saws) was born was uneducated and hence he(saws) remained that way. So, the great and noble Quran being revealed to such a person is surely a miracle unprecedented in history. That is why the Holy Quran challenges the disbelievers that if they do not believe the Holy Quran to be the word of God, then try to produce something similar to it:\n﴿قُل لَّئِنِ اجْتَمَعَتِ الْإِنسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلَىٰ أَن يَأْتُوا بِمِثْلِ هَـٰذَا الْقُرْآنِ لَا يَأْتُونَ بِمِثْلِهِ وَلَوْ كَانَ بَعْضُهُمْ لِبَعْضٍ ظَهِيرًا ٨٨﴾\nSay, \"If mankind and the jinn gathered in order to produce the like of this Qur'an, they could not produce the like of it, even if they were to each other assistants.\"\n[Bani-Israel: 88]\nThe polytheists and disbelievers of Makkah could not produce a book like the Holy Quran even though they considered themselves to be the greatest scholars of Arabic.\nAgain the Holy Quran challenges the disbelievers that if they cannot produce an entire book, then try producing a few similar verses at least:\n﴿أَمْ يَقُولُونَ افْتَرَاهُ ۖ قُلْ فَأْتُوا بِعَشْرِ سُوَرٍ مِّثْلِهِ مُفْتَرَيَاتٍ وَادْعُوا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُم مِّن دُونِ اللَّـهِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ١٣﴾\nOr do they say, \"He invented it\"? Say, \"Then bring ten surahs like it that have been invented and call upon [for assistance] whomever you can besides Allah, if you should be truthful.\"\n[Hud: 13]\nWhen the disbelievers could not even do that, the Quran challenges them a third time:\n﴿أَمْ يَقُولُونَ افْتَرَاهُ ۖ قُلْ فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِّثْلِهِ وَادْعُوا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُم مِّن دُونِ اللَّـهِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ٣٨﴾\nOr do they say [about the Prophet], \"He invented it?\" Say, \"Then bring forth a surah like it and call upon [for assistance] whomever you can besides Allah, if you should be truthful.\"\n[Yunus: 38]\nThis means that if the disbelievers consider the Holy Quran to be from someone other than Allah(swt), then produce just one verse like the ones in the Holy Quran and taking anybody’s help other than that of Allah(swt) if the disbelievers are indeed truthful.\nBut the disbelievers were unsuccessful even in this. Then the Holy Quran challenges them to produce at least one statement like that in the Holy Quran.\n﴿أَمْ يَقُولُونَ تَقَوَّلَهُ ۚ بَل لَّا يُؤْمِنُونَ ٣٣ فَلْيَأْتُوا بِحَدِيثٍ مِّثْلِهِ إِن كَانُوا صَادِقِينَ ٣٤﴾\nOr do they say, \"He has made it up\"? Rather, they do not believe. Then let them produce a statement like it, if they should be truthful.\n[At-Tur: 33-34]\n﴿وَإِن كُنتُمْ فِي رَيْبٍ مِّمَّا نَزَّلْنَا عَلَىٰ عَبْدِنَا فَأْتُوا بِسُورَةٍ مِّن مِّثْلِهِ وَادْعُوا شُهَدَاءَكُم مِّن دُونِ اللَّـهِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ٢٣﴾\nAnd if you are in doubt about what We have sent down upon Our Servant [Muhammad], then produce a surah the like thereof and call upon your witnesses other than Allah, if you should be truthful.\n[Al-Baqara: 23]\nHence the greatest miracle is the Holy Quran which was revealed to the Holy Prophet(saws) even though he could not read or write. The noble Quran has deeply influenced millions of people to date and shall continue to influence people till Doomsday and nobody has the capacity to produce something like it till the Last Day, other than Allah(swt).\nThe letters of the Holy Prophet(saws) to various kings:\nWe reproduce here a letter which the Holy Prophet(saws) had written to the king of Egypt and the reply to it.\nIn 9 A.H, the Holy Prophet(saws) wrote letters to many kings. Among them was the king of Egypt, Muqaqis. The letter written to him went as follows:\nFrom Muhammad Servant of Allah and His Prophet To Muqawqis, Vicegerent of Egypt Peace be on him who has taken the right course. Thereafter, I invite you to accept Islam. Therefore, if you want security, accept Islam. If you accept Islam, Allah, the Sublime, shall reward you doubly. But if you refuse to do so, responsibility for the transgression of the entire nation shall be yours.\nThen, he(saws) wrote the following verse from the Holy Quran:\nO people of the Book! Leaving aside all matters of difference and dispute, agree on a matter which is equally consistent between you and us and it is that we should not worship anyone except Allah and that we should neither associate anyone with Him,\nNor make anyone else as our god.\nIf you refuse it, you must know that we, in all circumstances, believe in Oneness of Allah.\nThe reply of king Muqaqis:\nTo Muhammad, son of Abdullah,\nFrom Muqawqis\n\"I read your letter and understood what you have written. I know that the coming of a Prophet is still due. But I thought, he would be born in Syria -- I have treated your messenger with respect and honour. I am sending two maids for you as presents. These maids belong to a very respectable family amongst us. In addition I send for you clothes and a duldul (steed) for riding. May Allah bestow security on you.'\"\nSome European scholars are of the opinion that the reply of Muqaqis was as follows:\n“In the name of Allah(swt), from Muhammad to Muqaqis. I received your letter. I have read it and understood whatever is in it. You say that Allah(swt) has sent you as His messenger and that the Quran has been revealed to you. In the light of our knowledge, it is clear to us that you are the one who invites people towards Allah(swt) and that you are one who speaks the truth. If I had not been the king of a vast country I would have been the first person to come to you. I am also aware that you are the seal of the prophets; that is, no other prophet shall come after you and that you are the king of prophets and the best among the people of good character.\nMay the blessings and peace of Allah(swt) be upon you till the Last Day.”\nOf the two maids described in the above letter, one was Mariah Khibtiya whom the Holy Prophet(saws) married and she gave birth to Ibraheem-bin-Muhammad. But very soon Ibraheem passed away. Upon that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n“My eyes are crying and my heart is heavy with grief, but even then I shall not say anything which may displease my Lord.”\nMuqaqis did not become a Muslim but in 21 A.H, during the time of Umar-bin-Khattab, Muslims won Egypt under the command of Abdullah-bin-Amr-bin-Aas and in a few years Islam had spread throughout Egypt.\nEgypt occupies a very important place in the history of Islam. Many prominent scholars were born there. It became the center of Quran and hadith commentators. The first university of the world was first established there about one thousand years back. Today it is known as ‘Jamia Azhar’. Even today thousands of scholars from this university are engaged in the propagation of Islam.\nThe letter from the Holy Prophet(saws) to the king Muqaqis is preserved in a museum in Istanbul."],[228,"§Muhammad(saws) and his daughters\nIn the Holy Quran, the daughters of Muhammad(saws) have also been described and they have been commanded to observe ‘purdah’ when they go out:\nيَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ قُل لِّأَزْوَاجِكَ وَبَنَاتِكَ وَنِسَاءِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ يُدْنِينَ عَلَيْهِنَّ مِن جَلَابِيبِهِنَّ ۚ\nO Prophet, tell your wives and your daughters and the women of the believers to bring down over themselves [part] of their outer garments.\n[Al-Ahzab: 59]\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) had four daughters and they were:\n1. Zainab:\nShe was the eldest among her sisters. During the lifetime of her mother Khadija itself she was married to her maternal aunt’s son Abul-Aas. She had a daughter named Umama (whom Ali(ra) married after the death of Fathima). She had a son named Ali who died in his childhood.\nZainab(ra) after becoming a Muslim migrated to Madina while her husband became a Muslim later on, some seven years after Zainab. It is narrated in the sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) held their marriage (Nikah) valid. We come to know from this that even though husband and wife do not accept Islam at the same time and there is a time gap, the original marriage remains valid. It is not necessary for them to get married again. But some scholars do not agree with this. They are of the opinion that if the husband becomes a Muslim before the waiting period (iddat) of the wife has elapsed, then it is not necessary for them to get married again but in case the waiting period has elapsed, it is necessary for them to get married again. It is narrated in Tirmizi and Ibn-Maaja that the Holy Prophet(saws) performed the remarriage of Zainab and Abul-Aas and decided the ‘meher’ or ‘dower’ again. (Tirmizi: 1142 and Ibn-Maaja: 2010). But in the case of this hadith the narration of one narrator ‘Hajjaj-bin-Arta’ is not reliable. During the life of the Holy Prophet(saws) itself, she passed away in 8 A.H.\n2. Ruqaiyya:\nShe was first married to Utba, the son of Abu-Lahab. Even though Abu-Lahab was the paternal uncle of Muhammad(saws), when he(saws) was made a prophet by Allah(swt), he became the worst enemy of the Holy Prophet(saws). So much so, that an entire surah was revealed cursing him. This is the surah Lahab. He compelled his son to divorce Ruqaiyya immediately. Then, she was married to Usman(ra) and they had a son named Abdullah who died in his childhood.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) had not yet returned to Madina from the battle of Badr, when Ruqaiyya passed away.\n3. Umme-Kulsum:\nShe was the third daughter of the Holy Prophet(saws). She was first married to Utaiba, the son of Abu-Lahab. But as she was quite young, she hadn’t yet gone to her husband’s place. Abu-Lahab compelled his son to divorce her. When her sister Ruqaiyya passed away, she was married to Usman(ra) in 3 A.H. But after six years, that is in 9 A.H, even she passed away. She did not have any children. It is narrated by Anas(ra) that he had seen the Holy Prophet(saws) sitting near the grave of Umme-Kulsum and that his eyes were filled with tears.\n4. Fathima:\nShe was the fourth and youngest daughter of the Holy Prophet(saws). Her mother was Khadija(ra). She was born a few years before the prophethood of Muhammad(saws). In 2 A.H, she was married to Ali(ra). Her children were Hasan, Hussain, Muhsin, Umme-Kulsum and Zainab(ra).\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was very fond of Fathima. Whenever she came to him, he(saws) would get up to welcome her and saying ‘my daughter’ he(saws) would stroke her head.\nWhen the time of the demise of the Holy Prophet(saws) was nearing, once Fathima came to him and upon seeing her he(saws) was very happy. He(saws) got up to welcome her and made her sit beside him. Then, the Holy Prophet(saws) told her something and she started crying and continued to do so for quite some time. Then, the Holy Prophet(saws) told her something and she was overjoyed and started laughing. After the Holy Prophet(saws) left, Aisha(ra) asked her, “Fathima, can you tell me why you cried first and then laughed with joy? What did the Holy Prophet(saws) tell you?” Fathima replied, ”It is a secret and I cannot disclose this secret of the Holy Prophet(saws) as he(saws) has told it to me in secret.” But after the death of the Holy Prophet(saws), Aisha(ra) again asked Fathima what it was that made her cry at first and then made her laugh.\nFathima(ra) replied, ”Yes, now I can reveal the secret as the Holy Prophet(saws) is no more. First the Holy Prophet(saws) gave me the sad news of his impending death and it made me cry. Seeing me cry, he(saws) said that among the members of his family, I shall be the first to join him and I started laughing with joy.” (Sahih Bukhari: 6285, 6286 and Sahih Muslim: 2450)\nSix months after the death of the Holy Prophet(saws), Fathima too passed away and she was twenty-three years old at the time."],[229,"§Muhammad(saws) and his wives\nIn the Arabic language, the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) are called ‘Azwaj-e-Mutaherat’.\nIn the Muslim society, the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) enjoy a very high and special position.\n1. It has been clearly mentioned in the Holy Quran that the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) are not like other ordinary women:\n﴿يَا نِسَاءَ النَّبِيِّ لَسْتُنَّ كَأَحَدٍ مِّنَ النِّسَاءِ ۚ إِنِ اتَّقَيْتُنَّ فَلَا تَخْضَعْنَ بِالْقَوْلِ فَيَطْمَعَ الَّذِي فِي قَلْبِهِ مَرَضٌ وَقُلْنَ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوفًا ٣٢﴾\nO wives of the Prophet, you are not like anyone among women. If you fear Allah, then do not be soft in speech [to men], lest he in whose heart is disease should covet, but speak with appropriate speech.\n[Al-Ahzab: 32]\n2. In the Holy Quran, the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) have been warned:\n﴿يَا نِسَاءَ النَّبِيِّ مَن يَأْتِ مِنكُنَّ بِفَاحِشَةٍ مُّبَيِّنَةٍ يُضَاعَفْ لَهَا الْعَذَابُ ضِعْفَيْنِ ۚ وَكَانَ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى اللَّـهِ يَسِيرًا ٣٠﴾\nO wives of the Prophet, whoever of you should commit a clear immorality - for her the punishment would be doubled two fold, and ever is that, for Allah, easy.\n[Al-Ahzab: 30]\n3. The wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) are like the mothers of the believers. The Holy Quran says:\nالنَّبِيُّ أَوْلَىٰ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ مِنْ أَنفُسِهِمْ ۖ وَأَزْوَاجُهُ أُمَّهَاتُهُمْ\nThe Prophet is more worthy of the believers than themselves, and his wives are [in the position of] their mothers.\n[Al-Ahzab: 6]\n4. That is why it is forbidden to marry the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws):\nوَمَا كَانَ لَكُمْ أَن تُؤْذُوا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَلَا أَن تَنكِحُوا أَزْوَاجَهُ مِن بَعْدِهِ أَبَدًا ۚ إِنَّ ذَٰلِكُمْ كَانَ عِندَ اللَّهِ عَظِيمًا\nAnd it is not [conceivable or lawful] for you to harm the Messenger of Allah or to marry his wives after him, ever. Indeed, that would be in the sight of Allah an enormity.\n[Al-Ahzab: 53]\nBy describing the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) as ‘Mothers of believers’ it is being stressed that they should be highly honoured. But, purdah must be observed. Thus, in this way it has been forbidden to marry the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) had twelve wives.\nThe ‘Antim Maharshi’ or the ‘Last Maharshi’ described in the Vedas and Puranas also has twelve wives. And no other messenger or rishi in history has twelve wives.(See: Antim Avatar: Vikashnand Brahmachari)\nBelow is presented a brief description of the twelve wives:\n1. Khadija(ra):\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) married Khadija when he(saws) was twenty-five. Khadija was a widow of forty. The name of her first husband was Abu-Haala and her second husband was Ateeq.\nWhen Allah(swt) made Muhammad(saws) a prophet, Khadija was the first woman to accept Islam. When the Holy Prophet(saws) was engaged in the remembrance of Allah(swt) in the cave Hira, Jibrail(as) appeared in front of him with the first revelation. The Holy Prophet(saws) was frightened at the time and rushed home shivering and narrated the whole thing to his wife. Calming down the Holy Prophet(saws), Khadija(ra) said, “I swear in the name of One in whose hand is the life of Khadija. You shall be the messenger of this ummah. You speak the truth, maintain the ties of kinship, take care of things entrusted to you, help the needy and poor, honour your guests, help others in good works. How can Allah(swt) destroy you?” Then she took Muhammad(saws) to her paternal cousin Waraqa-bin-Noufal, who had embraced Christianity and was studying the Injeel in Hebrew. When Khadija(ra) narrated whatever had happened, Waraqa said, ”This is the same messenger who had come to Musa(as). I wish I could be alive till the day your people drive you out of this place.” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Will my people drive me out of here?” Waraqa replied, ”Yes, whenever somebody like you has come, the people have tormented him. If I am alive till that day, I shall help you.” But Waraqa died a few days after this. (See: Sahih Bukhari: 3)\nThe children of Muhammad(saws) and Khadija(ra) were:\nThe sons Qasim, Tayyib and Tahir who died in their childhood and daughters Ruqaiyya, Zainab, Umme-Kulsum and Fathima(ra).\nKhadija(ra) passed away three years before the Holy Prophet(saws)’s migration from Makkah to Madina.\nAmong the many favours bestowed upon Khadija(ra), one was the place given to her in paradise. Once Jibrail(as) came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and said,\n“O Muhammad! When Khadija comes to you convey salaam to her from me and my Lord. And give her glad tidings of a mansion in paradise in which there will not be any disturbance nor will she feel any tiredness in it.” (Sahih Bukhari, 3820, Sahih Muslim, 2432)\n2. Sauda(ra):\nShe was the daughter of Jam’a-bin-Qais Quraishi. Her first husband was Sakran-bin-Amr. After embracing Islam, both of them went away to Ethiopia. Sakran died there itself. At the time Khadija(ra) had also died and hence the Holy Prophet(saws) married her in the 10th year of prophethood. She died in 54 A.H. (Tabqat Ibn-Sad, 8:53)\nSome people are of the opinion that she passed away in the last days of Caliph-hood of Umar(ra). (Taariq Kabir, 1:49-50)\n3. Aisha(ra):\nAll the women whom the Holy Prophet(saws) married were either divorcees or widows except Aisha(ra). The Holy Prophet(saws) loved her a lot. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that Aisha(ra) is superior to other women in the same way as a food item called ‘sareed’ is superior to other food items. (Sahih Bukhari, 3770 and Sahih Muslim, 2446)\nThe food sareed is popular among Arabs even today. This is made by grinding dates and wheat together and cooking them in ghee.\nAisha(ra) is a very prominent lady in Islamic history due to whom many hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws) have reached us. She is one of the ten main companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) who have narrated the sunnah of the Holy Prophet(saws) and about two thousand two hundred and ten hadith are attributed to her. She was with him when he(saws) passed away. The Holy Prophet(saws) was buried at her place itself. After the Holy Prophet(saws), she narrated many of his hadith, mainly the ones pertaining to his domestic life; that is his behavior towards his family members and marital life. She described in detail the different aspects of his life which is a role model for Muslims.\nShe passed away in 57 A.H, and was buried in Baqi.\n4. Hafsa(ra):\nShe was the daughter of Umar(ra). Her first husband was Rabunes-bin-Huzafa who was martyred in the war of Badr. Then she was married to the Holy Prophet(saws). Once when the Holy Prophet(saws) divorced her due to some reason, Jibrail(as) came to him and asked him to revoke the divorce because Hafsa was a very pious woman who fasted frequently and prayed during the nights. She will be the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws) even in paradise. (See: Abu Dawood, 2282; Nasai, 6:213)\nShe passed away in 41 A.H.\n5. Zainab(ra):\nShe was the daughter of Khuzaima-bin-Haaris. Her first husband was Ubaida-bin-Haaris who was martyred in the war of Badr. After the death of Haaris, Zainab(ra) was married to the Holy Prophet(saws). But just four months after the marriage she passed away in 4 A.H.\n6. Umme-Salma(ra):\nShe was the wife of Abu-Salma-bin-Abdul-Asad. After his death in 4 A.H, she was married to the Holy Prophet(saws). She was a widow with three children. The Holy Prophet(saws) helped out the widows by marrying them. And moreover, he(saws) wanted to spread Islam among the people of the tribes of his wives because it was the Arab custom that the people helped out those who were joined by ties of marriage. So, even the marriages of the Holy Prophet(saws) were a way of spreading Islam and for the good of Islam. Umme-Salma(ra) passed away in 59 A.H. and was buried in Baqi.\n7. Zainab(ra):\nShe was the wife of the adopted son of Muhammad(saws), Zaid. But it became impossible for them to live together and therefore Zaid divorced her. According to the Arab custom a person could not marry the widow or divorcee of his adopted son. An adopted son was considered equal in all respects to a biological son. But Islam does not permit this. So, following the command of Allah(swt), Muhammad(saws) married Zainab. In the beginning there was a great opposition to this and then the following verse was revealed:\nفَلَمَّا قَضَىٰ زَيْدٌ مِّنْهَا وَطَرًا زَوَّجْنَاكَهَا لِكَيْ لَا يَكُونَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ حَرَجٌ فِي أَزْوَاجِ أَدْعِيَائِهِمْ إِذَا قَضَوْا مِنْهُنَّ وَطَرًا ۚ\nSo when Zayd had no longer any need for her, We married her to you in order that there not be upon the believers any discomfort concerning the wives of their adopted sons when they no longer have need of them.\n[Al-Ahzab: 37]\nThus ended all opposition. And it became permissible to marry the widow or divorcee of one’s adopted son in Islam. This was why Zainab boasted that while the marriages of the other wives were performed by their family members, her marriage was performed by Allah(swt).\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said, “The one who spends the most in charity shall be the first to meet me.” Aisha(ra) would say that there were two good things about Zainab. One was that her marriage was performed by Allah(swt) and the second was that as the Holy Prophet(saws) had said, ”the one who gives the most in charity shall meet me first” and it was Zainab who died in 20 A.H.\n8. Juveria(ra):\nShe was the daughter of Haaris-bin-Abi-Zaraar. Her first husband was Safwan-bin-Zi Shakhar. The Holy Prophet(saws) married her in 6 A.H. and she died in 56 A.H.\n9. Umme-Habeeba(ra):\nShe was the daughter of one of the chieftains of Makkah, Abu-Sufyan. Her first husband was Ubaidullah-bin-Jahsh. Both of them migrated to Ethiopia after embracing Islam. But after going there, Ubaidullah became a Christian and started drinking alcohol. He died there itself. The king of Ethiopia Najashi married Umme-Habeeba to Muhammad(saws) taking a meher (dower) of four hundred dinars. When this news reached her father Abu-Sufyan, who had not yet accepted Islam, he said\n“He(saws) is such a leader whose name cannot be struck off” that is, such a great person is worthy of marrying my daughter.\nAbu-Sufyan who was a chieftain of Makkah and also a leader of the disbelievers could not deny the greatness of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nUmme-Habeeba(ra) passed away in 44 A.H. At that time her brother Mua’wiah was the caliph of the Muslims.\n10. Safia(ra):\nShe was the daughter of the Jewish chieftain Huyayy-bin-Aqtab. She was taken as a slave in the war of Khyber. Her first husband was Kanana who was killed in some war. After that the Holy Prophet(saws) married her. She proved to be a very wise and understanding woman. One day Hafsa(ra) taunted her saying that she was the daughter of a Jew. She became sad and started weeping. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know of this he(saws) told her, “You are the daughter of a prophet, your paternal uncle was a prophet and you are the wife of a prophet. So, how can they feel proud in comparison to you. And Hafsa, have fear of Allah(swt).” (Musnad Ahmad, 3:135)\nThis was true because she was the daughter of Huyayy-bin-Aqtab who was from the tribe of Haroon(as).\nShe died in 50 A.H. and was buried in Baqi.\n11. Maimoonah(ra):\nShe was first married to Masood-bin-Amr. He divorced her. She was then married to Abu-Raham-bin-Abdul-Uzza who passed away. After that she was married to the Holy Prophet(saws) in 7 A.H. She died at the age of 80 in 61 A.H. and was buried in a place called ‘Sarif’ near Makkah.\n12. Mariah Khibtiya(ra):\nShe was the daughter of Shamon of Egypt and was very beautiful. The king of Alexandria had given her as a gift to the Holy Prophet(saws). He(saws) had a great affection for her as she was the mother of his son Ibraheem, who died in his childhood.\nShe died in 14 A.H, and was buried in Baqi.\nSo, this was a brief description of the twelve wives of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nMention is also made of ‘Rehana-bint-Zaid’ who was also the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws) and was from the family of the Jew Banu-Quraija. After the war of Bani-Quraija, she came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and accepted Islam. Thereafter the Holy Prophet(saws) married her. She died in 10 A.H. A few more ladies are mentioned in the historical books, who were the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws). But they were either divorced or died before the Holy Prophet(saws) came home. For example: Alia-bint-Zam’an, Umaima-bint-Nauman, Qawla-bint-Huzail, Amra-bint-Zaid etc. Polygamy was the custom of those days. Even in the Bible, most of the prophets had more than one wife. Jesus did not marry during his life and so the Christian priests and nuns do not marry. They believe that after Doomsday all of them will marry Jesus. That is if a prophet remains unmarried all through his life, then in the next life he shall have a thousand wives. Islam does not say anything in this regard.\nIf we consider polygamy from a social point of view, we can understand that it is a necessity. Sometimes the need is individual and sometimes it is for the good of the society. It has been observed that in the societies and religions where polygamy is forbidden, adultery is prevalent because if a person cannot fulfill his desires in the legitimate way, he resorts to immoral conduct. When we study the societies in which widow-remarriage is forbidden, we come to know the atrocities committed in the name of religion. In the same way, the women outnumber the men in some societies. In such cases, polygamy offers a decent solution. For example, if a man has four daughters, he may find it difficult to marry them off in the absence of polygamy. In the societies where polygamy is allowed, the women are not at a loss as they are given the dower (meher) and then married.\nIt is due to these various reasons that Islam has allowed polygamy. But, a few rules have been laid down for this. Firstly, at any given time a man cannot have more than four wives. (See: Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-3)\nThe second rule is that he should deal with all of them justly. (See: Quran, Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-3)\nIn all matters like food and clothing, gifts, spending the days and nights etc. he should be just and impartial. If one is not capable of doing justice in all matters then he should marry only one woman and spend his life happily with her because if justice is not done between all the wives, then instead of being beneficial to the society, polygamy can create unrest and chaos which goes against the ultimate aim of polygamy."],[230,"§Mule\nA mule is smaller than a horse but bigger than a donkey. This is a cross between a horse and a donkey. This is a very patient but obstinate animal. This can be used in places where the horses cannot work; for example for climbing mountains and walking on rocky terrain. That is why the people living in the mountains of Lebanon use mules extensively.\nIn ancient times mules were used for riding. It has been forbidden in the Bible to keep the mule along with the other animals.\n(See: Bible, Lavi, 19:19)\nIt has been mentioned in the Bible that Sulaiman(as) would accept mules as gifts.\n(See: Kings, 10:25)\nIn the Holy Quran, reference is made to mules in connection with animals used for riding:\n﴿وَالْخَيْلَ وَالْبِغَالَ وَالْحَمِيرَ لِتَرْكَبُوهَا وَزِينَةً ۚ وَيَخْلُقُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ٨﴾\nAnd (He has created) horses, mules, and donkeys, for you to ride and use for show; and He has created (other) things of which ye have no knowledge.\n[An-Nahl: 8]"],[231,"§Murder\nAmong the things forbidden in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith, one is murder or unlawful killing.\n﴿وَمَن يَقْتُلْ مُؤْمِنًا مُّتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَاؤُهُ جَهَنَّمُ خَالِدًا فِيهَا وَغَضِبَ اللَّـهُ عَلَيْهِ وَلَعَنَهُ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُ عَذَابًا عَظِيمًا ٩٣﴾\nBut whoever kills a believer intentionally - his recompense is Hell, wherein he will abide eternally, and Allah has become angry with him and has cursed him and has prepared for him a great punishment.\n[An-Nisa: 93]\n﴿وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِي حَرَّمَ اللَّـهُ إِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ۗ وَمَن قُتِلَ مَظْلُومًا فَقَدْ جَعَلْنَا لِوَلِيِّهِ سُلْطَانًا فَلَا يُسْرِف فِّي الْقَتْلِ ۖ إِنَّهُ كَانَ مَنصُورًا ٣٣﴾\nAnd do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden, except by right. And whoever is killed unjustly - We have given his heir authority, but let him not exceed limits in [the matter of] taking life. Indeed, he has been supported [by the law].\n[Bani-Israel: 33]\nThat is, in retaliation only life can be taken for one murder and not wipe out the entire tribe as in earlier times:\n﴿وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا أَوْلَادَكُمْ خَشْيَةَ إِمْلَاقٍ ۖ نَّحْنُ نَرْزُقُهُمْ وَإِيَّاكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ قَتْلَهُمْ كَانَ خِطْئًا كَبِيرًا ٣١﴾\nAnd do not kill your children for fear of poverty. We provide for them and for you. Indeed, their killing is ever a great sin.\n[Bani-Israel: 31]\nBefore the advent of Islam, people would kill their children fearing poverty and in the modern times the same thing is being done in the guise of ‘family planning’. In this way we are going back to the dark and ignorant times of the pre-Islamic era.\nOne day a man came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and questioned him about major sins. The Holy Prophet(saws) replied:\n“Major sins are that you invoke someone other than Allah(swt) when He(swt) has created you and kill your children fearing that they will eat with you and to commit adultery with your neighbour’s wife.”\nThen the Holy Prophet(saws) recited the following verse of the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ لَا يَدْعُونَ مَعَ اللَّـهِ إِلَـٰهًا آخَرَ وَلَا يَقْتُلُونَ النَّفْسَ الَّتِي حَرَّمَ اللَّـهُ إِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ وَلَا يَزْنُونَ ۚ وَمَن يَفْعَلْ ذَٰلِكَ يَلْقَ أَثَامًا ٦٨﴾\nAnd those who do not invoke with Allah another deity or kill the soul which Allah has forbidden [to be killed], except by right, and do not commit unlawful sexual intercourse. And whoever should do that will meet a penalty.\n[Al-Furqan: 68]\n(See: Sahih Bukhari: 6861 and Sahih Muslim: 86)"],[232,"§Musa(as)\nMusa(as) has been described in great detail in the Holy Quran because his life highlights many religious teachings. For ease of understanding let us divide his life-span into three parts:\nFirst span (from birth to 40 years): What is known about this period is that Musa(as) was born in Egypt around 1527 B.C. The Pharaoh Rameses III was the ruler at that time and the astrologers predicted that he would be killed at the hands of a youth from the tribe of Bani-Israel. So he commanded two mid-wives ‘Sifra’ and ‘Kua’ to kill all the sons born to the Bani-Israel:\n﴿نَتْلُو عَلَيْكَ مِن نَّبَإِ مُوسَىٰ وَفِرْعَوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ لِقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ ٣ إِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ عَلَا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَجَعَلَ أَهْلَهَا شِيَعًا يَسْتَضْعِفُ طَائِفَةً مِّنْهُمْ يُذَبِّحُ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ وَيَسْتَحْيِي نِسَاءَهُمْ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِينَ ٤﴾\nWe recite to you from the news of Moses and Pharaoh in truth for a people who believe. Indeed, Pharaoh exalted himself in the land and made its people into factions, oppressing a sector among them, slaughtering their [newborn] sons and keeping their females alive. Indeed, he was of the corrupters.\n[Al-Qasas: 3, 4]\nWhen Musa(as) was born, his mother kept feeding him her milk for three months and kept him hidden. Then, when the secret could no longer be kept hidden, following the command of Allah(swt) she put the baby in a basket and set him afloat in the river Nile. The basket slowly drifted to the place where the family members of the Pharaoh were bathing. They fell in love with the child and took him home. It is said that the Pharaoh was not in favour of bringing the child home, but his wife made him agree to it saying that he would bring sunshine into their lives. As they did not have any sons, she wanted to adopt him. Musa(as)’s mother was missing her son terribly. By the command of Allah(swt), the baby Musa(as) would not have milk from any other woman. The wife of Pharaoh was worried on this account. Meanwhile, Miriam the elder sister of Musa(as) who had followed the basket saw the wife of Pharaoh take Musa(as) with her. She came to the palace and told the Pharaoh’s wife that she would bring a lady whose milk the baby would definitely drink. Then she brought her mother to the palace. In this way, Musa(as) was fed by his own mother but brought up in the palace of the Pharaoh. Now, his mother was also happy. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ أَنْ أَرْضِعِيهِ ۖ فَإِذَا خِفْتِ عَلَيْهِ فَأَلْقِيهِ فِي الْيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحْزَنِي ۖ إِنَّا رَادُّوهُ إِلَيْكِ وَجَاعِلُوهُ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ٧﴾\nAnd We inspired to the mother of Moses, \"Suckle him; but when you fear for him, cast him into the river and do not fear and do not grieve. Indeed, We will return him to you and will make him [one] of the messengers.\"\n[Al-Qasas: 7]\nIn the book ‘Exodus’ of the Taurah, a detailed description is given. (See: 2:5-10)\nMoses was being brought up in the palace of the Pharaoh and he imbibed knowledge in all fields. When he was forty years old, he had to leave Egypt, the details of which shall be given later. Thereafter he was made a prophet and messenger:\n﴿وَلَمَّا بَلَغَ أَشُدَّهُ وَاسْتَوَىٰ آتَيْنَاهُ حُكْمًا وَعِلْمًا ۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ ١٤﴾\nAnd when he attained his full strength and was [mentally] mature, We bestowed upon him judgement and knowledge. And thus do We reward the doers of good.\n[Al-Qasas: 14]\nFrom this verse we do not come to know the number of years he spent in Egypt, but we understand from some verses of the Bible that he was in Egypt for forty years.But even in the Bible we do not get the complete details.\nSecond span: This starts from the time Musa(as) was forty years old. One day a fight broke out between a Qibti (Egyptian) and a Bani-Israelite. The Bani-Israelite complained about the Qibti to Musa(as). Musa(as) punched him due to which the Qibti died. (See: Quran, Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verse-15)\nMusa(as) fled to the city of Madyan after crossing the desert of Sina. It is mentioned in the book ‘Exodus’ of the Taurah that the Pharaoh decided to kill Musa(as) due to which he fled to Madyan.\nIn Madyan he reached a well where the shepherds came for water for their cattle and sheep. There he saw two girls waiting for water for their goats. After some time one of them came up to him shyly and said, “My father is calling you.” Musa(as) went to the house of the priest of Madyan. Some scholars are of the opinion that he was Shuaib(as). But this is not true. The priest was very pleased on seeing Musa(as) and Musa(as) narrated his entire story to him. The priest said, “If you serve me for eight years, I shall let you wed one of my daughters and if you serve me for ten years, it will be a favour from you.” (See: Quran, Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verses-24-29)\nAfter the service-period, Musa(as) was going along with his wife one day when he saw a fire burning in the valley of Tuwa, on Mount Tur. He told his wife that he would get some fire from there and also ask for directions. He went into the valley leaving his wife there itself. There he heard a voice:\n﴿فَلَمَّا أَتَاهَا نُودِيَ يَا مُوسَىٰ ١١ إِنِّي أَنَا رَبُّكَ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَيْكَ ۖ إِنَّكَ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى ١٢ وَأَنَا اخْتَرْتُكَ فَاسْتَمِعْ لِمَا يُوحَىٰ ١٣ إِنَّنِي أَنَا اللَّـهُ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا أَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِي وَأَقِمِ الصَّلَاةَ لِذِكْرِي ١٤﴾\nAnd when he came to it, he was called, \"O Moses, Indeed, I am your Lord, so remove your sandals. Indeed, you are in the sacred valley of Tuwa. And I have chosen you, so listen to what is revealed [to you]. Indeed, I am Allah. There is no deity except Me, so worship Me and establish prayer for My remembrance.\n[Ta-Ha: 11-14]\nThen, he received the command to go to the Pharaoh who was spreading mischief on earth and instill the fear of Allah(swt) in his heart. Musa(as) begged Allah(swt) to make his brother Haroon(as) also a messenger so that he could help Musa(as) in his mission. Allah(swt) granted his wish and made Haroon(as) also a messenger. Then Allah(swt) gave Musa(as) nine miracles which are described as follows in the Holy Quran:\nوَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا مُوسَىٰ تِسْعَ آيَاتٍ بَيِّنَاتٍ\nAnd We had certainly given Moses nine evident signs.\n[Bani-Israel: 101]\nA detailed description of these nine signs is given in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الطُّوفَانَ وَالْجَرَادَ وَالْقُمَّلَ وَالضَّفَادِعَ وَالدَّمَ آيَاتٍ مُّفَصَّلَاتٍ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا وَكَانُوا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِينَ ١٣٣﴾\nSo We sent upon them the flood and locusts and lice and frogs and blood as distinct signs, but they were arrogant and were a criminal people.\n[Al-A’raf: 133]\nFive signs are described in the above verse:\n1. Flood: Flood or cyclone is a heavy downpour accompanied by violent waves in the ocean and heavy winds. The flood described in the above verse was so powerful that the river Nile was overflowing drowning all the fields and livestock. It was a great calamity for the people of Egypt. There was death and destruction everywhere.\n2. Locusts: Allah(swt) sent a swarm of locusts upon the people of Egypt which did not spare anything in their path. They either ate it up or destroyed it.\n3. Lice: In the Holy Quran, the word ‘Qummal’ is used which are often found in the hair of humans. These cause many problems for humans.\n4. Frogs: It is said that there were suddenly so many frogs in Egypt that they were to be found everywhere causing great distress to the people.\n5. Blood: It is said that when they collected water from river Nile it would turn to blood and in the same way whenever they tried to drink water it would change to blood.\nAll these problems were faced by the people of Egypt. But the Bani-Israel were spared and they did not encounter any of these difficulties. These were the miraculous signs of Allah(swt) in order to make the people turn to the straight path and give up disbelief. The other four signs have been described in other places. They are:\nAsa or staff: Musa(as) had a staff which he used to graze the cattle and sheep. He was not aware that even that was a sign. As soon as he threw the staff on the ground, it turned into a great big snake and ate up the false snakes of the other magicians. But Musa(as) was not aware of this. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ ١٧ قَالَ هِيَ عَصَايَ أَتَوَكَّأُ عَلَيْهَا وَأَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلَىٰ غَنَمِي وَلِيَ فِيهَا مَآرِبُ أُخْرَىٰ ١٨ قَالَ أَلْقِهَا يَا مُوسَىٰ ١٩ فَأَلْقَاهَا فَإِذَا هِيَ حَيَّةٌ تَسْعَىٰ ٢٠ قَالَ خُذْهَا وَلَا تَخَفْ ۖ سَنُعِيدُهَا سِيرَتَهَا الْأُولَىٰ ٢١﴾\nAnd what is that in your right hand, O Moses?\" He said, \"It is my staff; I lean upon it, and I bring down leaves for my sheep and I have therein other uses.\" [Allah] said, \"Throw it down, O Moses.\" So he threw it down, and thereupon it was a snake, moving swiftly. [Allah] said, \"Seize it and fear not; We will return it to its former condition.\n[Ta-Ha: 17-21]\nYede-Baiza: This means ‘shining hand’. One other sign which Musa(as) was given was that when he put his hand under his arm and drew it out, it came out shining with white light. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَاضْمُمْ يَدَكَ إِلَىٰ جَنَاحِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَاءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوءٍ آيَةً أُخْرَىٰ ٢٢﴾\nAnd draw in your hand to your side; it will come out white without disease - another sign.\n[Ta-Ha: 22]\nIt is described at another place as:\n﴿وَنَزَعَ يَدَهُ فَإِذَا هِيَ بَيْضَاءُ لِلنَّاظِرِينَ ٣٣﴾\nAnd he drew out his hand; thereupon it was white for the observers.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 33]\nSineen: This means famine. There was a severe famine in Egypt for many years due to which there was no vegetation and people started dying of hunger.\n﴿وَلَقَدْ أَخَذْنَا آلَ فِرْعَوْنَ بِالسِّنِينَ وَنَقْصٍ مِّنَ الثَّمَرَاتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَذَّكَّرُونَ ١٣٠﴾\nAnd We certainly seized the people of Pharaoh with years of famine and a deficiency in fruits that perhaps they would be reminded.\n[Al-A’raf: 130]\nThese are the signs with which Allah(swt) sent His(swt) prophet Musa(as) to the Pharaoh and his tribe to invite them to the worship of the One True Allah(swt). But the Pharaoh and his tribe were indeed very strange. Whenever some calamity befell them, they would rush to Musa(as) and say:\n﴿وَلَمَّا وَقَعَ عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّجْزُ قَالُوا يَا مُوسَى ادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ بِمَا عَهِدَ عِندَكَ ۖ لَئِن كَشَفْتَ عَنَّا الرِّجْزَ لَنُؤْمِنَنَّ لَكَ وَلَنُرْسِلَنَّ مَعَكَ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ ١٣٤﴾\n\"O Moses, invoke for us your Lord by what He has promised you. If you [can] remove the punishment from us, we will surely believe you, and we will send with you the Children of Israel.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 134]\nBut they did nothing of the sort. Whenever the calamity was removed they went back to their old ways:\n﴿فَلَمَّا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمُ الرِّجْزَ إِلَىٰ أَجَلٍ هُم بَالِغُوهُ إِذَا هُمْ يَنكُثُونَ ١٣٥﴾\nBut when We removed the punishment from them until a term which they were to reach, then at once they broke their word.\n[Al-A’raf: 135]\nIn the Holy Quran, Allah(swt) describes a dialogue which took place between Musa(as) and the Pharaoh:\n﴿الَ فَمَن رَّبُّكُمَا يَا مُوسَىٰ ٤٩ قَالَ رَبُّنَا الَّذِي أَعْطَىٰ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ خَلْقَهُ ثُمَّ هَدَىٰ ٥٠ قَالَ فَمَا بَالُ الْقُرُونِ الْأُولَىٰ ٥١ قَالَ عِلْمُهَا عِندَ رَبِّي فِي كِتَابٍ ۖ لَّا يَضِلُّ رَبِّي وَلَا يَنسَى ٥٢﴾\n[Pharaoh] said, \"So who is the Lord of you two, O Moses?\" He said, \"Our Lord is He who gave each thing its form and then guided [it].\" [Pharaoh] said, \"Then what is the case of the former generations?\" [Moses] said, \"The knowledge thereof is with my Lord in a record. My Lord neither errs nor forgets.\"\n[Ta-Ha: 49-52]\nWhen the Pharaoh could not understand anything, he started threatening Musa(as):\n﴿قَالَ أَجِئْتَنَا لِتُخْرِجَنَا مِنْ أَرْضِنَا بِسِحْرِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ ٥٧ فَلَنَأْتِيَنَّكَ بِسِحْرٍ مِّثْلِهِ﴾\nHe said, \"Have you come to us to drive us out of our land with your magic, O Moses? Then we will surely bring you magic like it.\n[Ta-Ha: 57, 58]\nIn the end, the festival day was decided upon for the duel between the two. The magicians of the Pharaoh said, “O Musa! Will you show your magic first or shall we?” Musa(as) asked them to throw first. He saw the staffs and ropes of the magicians moving about like snakes. Following the command of Allah(swt), Musa(as) threw down his staff which turned into a huge snake and started eating up the false snakes of the magicians. Seeing this miracle all the magicians fell down in prostration and said, “We believe in the Lord of Haroon and Moses.” Seeing this the Pharaoh was furious and said, “You have believed before I gave you permission. I shall chop off your hands and feet and crucify you on the trunks of palm trees.” But they had become firm believers. They said unanimously:\n﴿قَالُوا لَن نُّؤْثِرَكَ عَلَىٰ مَا جَاءَنَا مِنَ الْبَيِّنَاتِ وَالَّذِي فَطَرَنَا ۖ فَاقْضِ مَا أَنتَ قَاضٍ ۖ إِنَّمَا تَقْضِي هَـٰذِهِ الْحَيَاةَ الدُّنْيَا ٧٢﴾\nThey said, \"Never will we prefer you over what has come to us of clear proofs and [over] He who created us. So decree whatever you are to decree. You can only decree for this worldly life.\n[Ta-Ha: 72]\nAt another place in the Holy Quran, this same incident is described as:\n﴿وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ أَنْ أَلْقِ عَصَاكَ ۖ فَإِذَا هِيَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَأْفِكُونَ ١١٧ فَوَقَعَ الْحَقُّ وَبَطَلَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ١١٨ فَغُلِبُوا هُنَالِكَ وَانقَلَبُوا صَاغِرِينَ ١١٩ وَأُلْقِيَ السَّحَرَةُ سَاجِدِينَ ١٢٠ قَالُوا آمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ١٢١ رَبِّ مُوسَىٰ وَهَارُونَ ١٢٢﴾\nAnd We inspired to Moses, \"Throw your staff,\" and at once it devoured what they were falsifying. So the truth was established, and abolished was what they were doing. And Pharaoh and his people were overcome right there and became debased. And the magicians fell down in prostration [to Allah]. They said, \"We have believed in the Lord of the worlds, The Lord of Moses and Aaron.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 117-122]\nBut this was not liked by the Pharaoh who threatened to cut off their hands and feet and hang them upside down. But the truth is that when someone becomes a believer in the true sense, he does not fear any mortal. The Pharaoh, in spite of all these signs did not become a believer:\n﴿فَكَذَّبَ وَعَصَىٰ ٢١ ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ يَسْعَىٰ ٢٢ فَحَشَرَ فَنَادَىٰ ٢٣ فَقَالَ أَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْأَعْلَىٰ ٢٤ فَأَخَذَهُ اللَّـهُ نَكَالَ الْآخِرَةِ وَالْأُولَىٰ ٢٥﴾\nBut Pharaoh denied and disobeyed. Then he turned his back, striving. And he gathered [his people] and called out .And said, \"I am your most exalted lord.\" So Allah seized him in exemplary punishment for the last and the first [transgression].\n[An-Nazi’at: 21-25]\nWhen the atrocities of the Pharaoh became unbearable, Allah(swt) commanded Musa(as) to leave Egypt along with the Bani-Israel. When the Pharaoh came to know about this he followed Musa(as) and his tribe with a huge army till the shores of the Red sea. There were tall mountains on either side of the sea. The Bani-Israel panicked because they had no escape-route – on one side was the sea and on the other the army of the Pharaoh. But Musa(as) was calm and composed because he had done what Allah(swt) had commanded him to do. Then, Allah(swt) performed a miracle:\n﴿فَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ أَنِ اضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ الْبَحْرَ ۖ فَانفَلَقَ فَكَانَ كُلُّ فِرْقٍ كَالطَّوْدِ الْعَظِيمِ ٦٣ وَأَزْلَفْنَا ثَمَّ الْآخَرِينَ ٦٤ وَأَنجَيْنَا مُوسَىٰ وَمَن مَّعَهُ أَجْمَعِينَ ٦٥ ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا الْآخَرِينَ ٦٦﴾\nThen We inspired to Moses, \"Strike with your staff the sea,\" and it parted, and each portion was like a great towering mountain. And We advanced thereto the pursuers. And We saved Moses and those with him, all together. Then We drowned the others.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 63-66]\nAt another place it says that twelve paths were formed in the sea because the Bani-Israel were divided into twelve groups. Between the groups there was a towering wall of water so that the Bani-Israel could cross over easily. So, in this way when the water had moved away creating a dry path, Musa(as) and his people started crossing the sea. Seeing this, the Pharaoh also followed with his huge army. Then, after the Bani-Israel had crossed over safely and the Pharaoh was still on the path in the sea, the water closed over and drowned the army along with the Pharaoh. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَأَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ بِجُنُودِهِ فَغَشِيَهُم مِّنَ الْيَمِّ مَا غَشِيَهُمْ ٧٨﴾\nSo Pharaoh pursued them with his soldiers, and there covered them from the sea that which covered them.\n[Ta-Ha: 78]\nNow the Pharaoh started believing in the prophethood of Musa(as) and also in the Oneness of Allah(swt) towards which Musa(as) was inviting. It is narrated in the sahih hadith that when a person starts believing when he knows he is about to die, his belief and repentance shall not be accepted from him. So, the repentance and belief of the Pharaoh was useless at this late stage:\n﴿وَجَاوَزْنَا بِبَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ الْبَحْرَ فَأَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ وَجُنُودُهُ بَغْيًا وَعَدْوًا ۖ حَتَّىٰ إِذَا أَدْرَكَهُ الْغَرَقُ قَالَ آمَنتُ أَنَّهُ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا الَّذِي آمَنَتْ بِهِ بَنُو إِسْرَائِيلَ وَأَنَا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ ٩٠ آلْآنَ وَقَدْ عَصَيْتَ قَبْلُ وَكُنتَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِينَ ٩١ فَالْيَوْمَ نُنَجِّيكَ بِبَدَنِكَ لِتَكُونَ لِمَنْ خَلْفَكَ آيَةً ۚ وَإِنَّ كَثِيرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِ عَنْ آيَاتِنَا لَغَافِلُونَ ٩٢﴾\nAnd We took the Children of Israel across the sea, and Pharaoh and his soldiers pursued them in tyranny and enmity until, when drowning overtook him, he said, \"I believe that there is no deity except that in whom the Children of Israel believe, and I am of the Muslims.\" Now? And you had disobeyed [Him] before and were of the corrupters? So today We will save you in body that you may be to those who succeed you a sign. And indeed, many among the people, of Our signs, are heedless.\n[Yunus: 90-92]\nSome scholars are of the opinion that the Bani-Israel could not believe that the Pharaoh was actually dead as they had been under his spell of power for so long that they had started considering him invincible. In the same way, the tribe of the Pharaoh also could not believe that he was dead as they had started considering him their god and hence immortal. To rid the people of these superstitions, Allah(swt) caused the corpse of the Pharaoh to be thrown onto the shore so that everybody could see the fate of their immortal god.\nTherefore, the Pharaoh was drowned along with his army and his belief at the last moment did not avail him. For a detailed description see ‘Pharaoh(Firaun).’ The Jews celebrate this event as a festival.\nIt is narrated in the Sahih Bukhari by Abdullah-bin-Abbas that when the Holy Prophet(saws) came to Madina, he(saws) saw that the Jews there were fasting on the 10th day of Muharram. The Holy Prophet(saws) asked: “What is this fast?” He(saws) got the reply that this was the day the Bani-Israel were freed from the Pharaoh.” The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “Even you fast on this day as you have a greater right to it than them.” (See: Sahih Bukhari -111)\nIn this way, Musa(as) crossed over to the other side of the Red sea and entered the desert. With this the second phase of his life comes to an end.\nThird span: Musa(as) entered the desert of Sina along with the Bani-Israel after crossing the Red sea. According to the Bible their number was more than six lakhs. But this does not appear to be true in the light of the following facts. Yaqub(as) along with his sons and grandsons who had come to Egypt numbered seventy. Imran was the son of his grandson Khahat. And Musa(as) and Haroon(as) were the sons of Imran. So, after Yaqub(as), only two generations lived in Egypt. So, it is impossible to have six lakh offspring from seventy people after just two generations.\nTherefore, the author of Encyclopedia of Britannica is of the opinion that the number was not more than fifteen thousand. (Part: 12, p.489). This is corroborated by the Holy Quran:\n﴿فَأَرْسَلَ فِرْعَوْنُ فِي الْمَدَائِنِ حَاشِرِينَ ٥٣ إِنَّ هَـٰؤُلَاءِ لَشِرْذِمَةٌ قَلِيلُونَ ٥٤ وَإِنَّهُمْ لَنَا لَغَائِظُونَ ٥٥﴾\nThen Pharaoh sent among the cities gatherers. [And said], \"Indeed, those are but a small band, And indeed, they are enraging us.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 53-55]\nThe word ‘Shirzimah’ is used for them in the Holy Quran which means ‘a small group.’\nThere is a difference of opinion even in the date of the exodus from Egypt. From the relics found during the excavations of Sina, it can be understood that the Bani-Israel came out during the reign of Minfatah(1527 – 1427 B.C), who was the son of Ramases II.(See: Ahmad Badavi: Maukiv shams-2, p.912)\nLet us now have a look at the important events which took place in the desert of Sina:\nThe desert of Sina is very hot with hardly any vegetation. The first miracle was that the clouds formed a cool cover for the Bani-Israel and Allah(swt) sent down Manna and Salwa for their sustenance.\n(See: Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-57)\nAs there was no water, by the command of Allah(swt), Musa(as) struck the ground with his staff and twelve springs burst forth so that the twelve groups of Bani-Israel could each take water from a spring. (See : Quran, Surah-Al-Baqara,Verse-60)\nWhen the Bani-Israel reached the desert of Sina they found some people worshipping idols. So, they asked Musa(as) also to make an idol for them so that they could worship it. Hearing this Musa(as) was deeply saddened because he was inviting people to the worship of the One True Allah(swt) which was also the essential message of all the other prophets. So, he said to his people, “You are behaving ignorantly.”(See: Quran, Surah-7, Verse-138)\nFollowing the command of Allah(swt), Musa(as) went to the mountain Tur and for forty days he was engaged in the remembrance of Allah(swt) and talking to Him(swt). Then he wished to have a glimpse of Allah(swt). Allah(swt) said, “You will not be able to see Me. So, look towards the mountain and if it remains standing, then you can see Me.” So, when his Lord appeared to the mountain, it was razed to the ground and Musa(as) fell down unconscious. After regaining consciousness, he started singing the praises of his Lord and repented for his behavior.(See: Quran, Surah-7, Verses-143,144)\nAfter the completion of forty days, Allah(swt) gave Musa(as) the tablets which had essential instructions for the Bani-Israel.\n(See: Quran, Surah-7, Al-A’raf, Verse-145)\nWhen Musa(as) came back to his tribe he found them worshipping a golden calf which they themselves had made. Musa(as) was furious and threw down the tablets. When he had calmed down he picked up the tablets which had the commandments of Allah(swt) for the guidance of people.\nNow it was time for the Bani-Israel to proceed to the sacred place which was promised to them by Allah(swt). But the Bani-Israel turned out to be cowards. They refused to enter Palestine saying that there were powerful people there and unless and until those people came out they would not enter it. So, Allah(swt) left them to wander in the desert for forty years. Musa(as) and Haroon(as) died there and so did the majority of Bani-Israel who had come from Egypt. When the new generation came of age, they entered the sacred land of Palestine along with Yusha-bin-Noon and thus the promise of Allah(swt) was fulfilled.\nMusa(as) was sent as a messenger to the Bani-Israel:\nوَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِ يَا قَوْمِ لِمَ تُؤْذُونَنِي وَقَد تَّعْلَمُونَ أَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ إِلَيْكُمْ\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when Moses said to his people, \"O my people, why do you harm me while you certainly know that I am the messenger of Allah to you?\"\n[As-Saff: 5]\nMusa(as) was tormented by the people of his tribe which is described again and again in the Holy Quran. This is corroborated in the Bible also. (See: Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verses 51-55; Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-153 and Surah-61, As-Saff, Verse-5). (Exodus, 5:2-12; Numbers, 11:1-15)\nThe message of Isa(as) was also for the Bani-Israel and he was the last messenger sent to the Bani-Israel:\nوَإِذْ قَالَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ يَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ إِنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ إِلَيْكُم مُّصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيَّ مِنَ التَّوْرَاةِ\nAnd [mention] when Jesus, the son of Mary, said, \"O children of Israel, indeed I am the messenger of Allah to you confirming what came before me of the Torah.\n[As-Saff: 6]\nFrom this we understand the following:\nIsa(as) was sent as a prophet to the Bani-Israel and not to the entire humanity as the Christians believe and with this belief they go to every corner of the world to spread Christianity.\nIsa(as) was a true prophet and not a liar as the Jews say.\nIsa(as) was a messenger and slave of Allah(swt) and is not someone to be worshipped as the Christians seem to think.\nIsa(as) gave glad tidings of a prophet who was to come after him called Ahmad because the Torah which was confirmed by him did not have all the rules for a life of truth. This prophet, whose coming was prophesied by Isa(as) is none other than Muhammad(saws) and the religion propagated by him is the guidance for the entire mankind.\nTherefore just as Isa(as) was the last prophet for the Bani-Israel, Muhammad(saws) is the last prophet for the entire mankind and no other prophet will come till Doomsday."],[233,"§Musa(as) and his sister\nMusa(as)’s sister has been described in two places in the Holy Quran but neither the Holy Quran nor the sahih hadith mentions her name.\nThe story goes as follows. When Musa(as) was born, there was a command from Allah(swt) to cast him away in the river Nile in a basket as the Pharaoh was killing all new-born males. Musa(as)’s mother was very sad about this but this was the wish of Allah(swt):\n﴿وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ أَنْ أَرْضِعِيهِ ۖ فَإِذَا خِفْتِ عَلَيْهِ فَأَلْقِيهِ فِي الْيَمِّ وَلَا تَخَافِي وَلَا تَحْزَنِي ۖ إِنَّا رَادُّوهُ إِلَيْكِ وَجَاعِلُوهُ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ٧﴾\nAnd We inspired to the mother of Moses, \"Suckle him; but when you fear for him, cast him into the river and do not fear and do not grieve. Indeed, We will return him to you and will make him [one] of the messengers.\"\n[Al-Qasas: 7]\nMusa(as)’s mother put him in a basket and set it afloat in the river and told his sister:\n﴿وَقَالَتْ لِأُخْتِهِ قُصِّيهِ ۖ فَبَصُرَتْ بِهِ عَن جُنُبٍ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ١١﴾\nAnd she said to his sister, \"Follow him\"; so she watched him from a distance while they perceived not.\n[Al-Qasas: 11]\n(See also: Bible, Exodus -2:4)\nAllah(swt) forbade any other woman’s milk for the baby Musa(as) and so the wife of the Pharaoh who had picked up the baby from the basket did not know how to feed the baby. So, Musa(as)’s sister said to her:\nهَلْ أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ أَهْلِ بَيْتٍ يَكْفُلُونَهُ لَكُمْ وَهُمْ لَهُ نَاصِحُونَ\n\"Shall I direct you to a household that will be responsible for him for you while they are to him [for his upbringing] sincere?\"\n[Al-Qasas: 12]\n(See also: Bible, Exodus 2:7)\nIn this way Allah(swt) restored Musa(as) to his mother and she was relieved from the pain of separation.\nAt another place in the Holy Quran, this is described as follows:\nإِذْ تَمْشِي أُخْتُكَ فَتَقُولُ هَلْ أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ مَن يَكْفُلُهُ\n[And We favored you] when your sister went and said, 'Shall I direct you to someone who will be responsible for him?'\n[Ta-Ha: 40]\nIn the Bible, Amram (father of Moses) is mentioned as having three children – Haroon, Moses and Miriam.(Bible, 1 Chronicles, 6:3)\nWe do not come to know the age of Musa(as)’s sister from the Bible. But we can guess that she must have been about fifteen years older than Musa(as). When the Pharaoh was drowned along with his army, it was this same Miriam who came out of Egypt along with the other ladies of Bani-Israel.\nThen Miriam the prophet, Aaron’s sister, took a timbrel in her hand, and all the women followed her, with timbrels and dancing. Miriam sang to them:\n“Sing to the Lord for He is highly exalted. Both horse and driver he has hurled into the sea.”\n(Bible, Exodus, 15:20-21)\nWhen Musa(as) married a Cushite lady, this was the same Miriam who started talking against Musa(as) and for this sin Allah(swt) made her skin leprous. When Musa(as) came to know about this he prayed to Allah(swt) and she was cured. (See: Bible, Numbers, 12:1-13)\nAfter coming out of Egypt, in the first month the whole Israelite community arrived in the desert of Sina and started staying in a place called Kadesh. Miriam died and was buried there.\n(See: Bible, Numbers, 20:1)"],[234,"§Nabi\n‘Nabi’ is one who gives a message or news. A ‘Nabi’ gives a message which is hidden from ordinary mortals and hence he is called ‘Nabi’. This message can either be something which our sense organs cannot perceive or something about the future.\n(For more information see ‘Rasool’)\nAfter the creation of mankind, Allah(swt) did not just leave them to wander around blindly, but sent down a chain of prophets for its guidance. There have been prophets sent to different parts of the world to different tribes at different times. The Holy Quran says:\nوَلِكُلِّ قَوْمٍ هَادٍ\nand for every people is a guide.\n[Ar-Ra’d: 7]\nAs these prophets were for the guidance of men, they themselves were humans and spoke the language of humans. They made the message of Allah(swt) clear to men and their life was a model for the others to follow. The Holy Quran says:\nوَمَا أَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ إِلَّا إِنَّهُمْ لَيَأْكُلُونَ الطَّعَامَ وَيَمْشُونَ فِي الْأَسْوَاقِ\nAnd We did not send before you, [O Muhammad], any of the messengers except that they ate food and walked in the markets.\n[Al-Furqan: 20]\nوَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلًا مِّن قَبْلِكَ وَجَعَلْنَا لَهُمْ أَزْوَاجًا وَذُرِّيَّةً\nAnd We have already sent messengers before you and assigned to them wives and descendants.\n[Ar-Ra’d: 38]\nThese verses disprove the view that Allah(swt) takes human form and comes down to earth. This also says that it is only Allah(swt) who makes someone a prophet and no one can claim prophethood of his own free will:\n﴿اللَّـهُ يَصْطَفِي مِنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ رُسُلًا وَمِنَ النَّاسِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ سَمِيعٌ بَصِيرٌ ٧٥﴾\nAllah chooses from the angels messengers and from the people. Indeed, Allah is Hearing and Seeing.\n[Al-Hajj: 75]\nMessenger from among the angels means ‘Jibrail(as)’ who brought divine revelations from Allah(swt) to the Holy Prophet(saws). Allah(swt) had chosen Jibrail(as) for this purpose.In the same way Allah(swt) chose Adam(as), Nuh(as), Ibraheem(as) etc. as prophets for their specific tribes and Muhammad(saws) in the end was sent as a prophet for the entire mankind. Muhammad(as) was the last prophet as no other prophet shall come after him.\n﴿مَّا كَانَ مُحَمَّدٌ أَبَا أَحَدٍ مِّن رِّجَالِكُمْ وَلَـٰكِن رَّسُولَ اللَّـهِ وَخَاتَمَ النَّبِيِّينَ ۗ وَكَانَ اللَّـهُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عَلِيمًا ٤٠﴾\nMuhammad is not the father of [any] one of your men, but [he is] the Messenger of Allah and last of the prophets. And ever is Allah, of all things, Knowing.\n[Al-Ahzab: 40]\nThis is also corroborated in a sahih hadith in which the Holy Prophet(saws) says that no other prophet shall come after him. That is, he is the last link in the chain of prophets and the religion brought by him is the last religion and the book brought by him namely the Holy Quran will be the guidance for mankind till Doomsday.\nThe difference between a ‘Nabi’ and ‘Rasool’ is that a ‘Rasool’ brings his own ‘shariat’ or ‘divine law’ while a ‘Nabi’ is sent to reinforce the ‘shariat’ of the previous ‘Rasool’."],[235,"§Nabi(saws) and his daughters\nSee: Muhammad(saws) and his daughters."],[236,"§Nabi(saws) and his wives\nSee: Muhammad(saws) and his wives."],[237,"§Nafil\n‘Nafil’ means ‘more’; that is something more than what is compulsory. For example when Ibraheem(as) prayed to Allah(swt) for a son, Allah(swt) granted him Ishaq(as) in addition to Ismael(as) and then Yaqub(as) was born to Ishaq(as) and both Yaqub(as) and Ishaq(as) were made prophets. (See: Quran,Surah-21, Al-Anbiya, Verse-72)\nIsmael(as) is not described in this verse as he was born fourteen years earlier. In another verse it says:\nوَمِنَ اللَّيْلِ فَتَهَجَّدْ بِهِ نَافِلَةً لَّكَ عَسَىٰ\nAnd from [part of] the night, pray with it as additional [worship] for you.\n[Bani-Israel: 79]\nThe Islamic injunctions which are compulsory or obligatory are called ‘Farz’ or ‘Wajib’ and if not followed they come under ‘major sins’. The other injunctions are called ‘Mujtahab’ and ‘Mandoob’. There is no sin in not doing them but doing them earns rewards.\nThis applies to various everyday activities as well as to various forms of worship. Some are being described as follows:\n1. After the ‘farz’ salahs every day, twelve rakat are ‘nafil’ and these are termed ‘Sunnat-e-Muakkaadah’. It is narrated in one sahih hadith that if a person offers these twelve rakat during the day and night, then a house will be built for him in paradise.\n(See: Sahih Muslim, 728)\nThese twelve rakats are as follows:\ntwo rakat before the ‘fazr’ salah\nfour rakat before the ‘zuhur’ salah\ntwo rakat after the ‘zuhur’ salah\ntwo rakat after the ‘maghrib’ salah\ntwo rakat after the ‘Isha’ salah\n2. After the obligatory zakat, ‘nafil’ charity has great importance. It is narrated in one sahih hadith that on the Day of Resurrection, seven types of people will be under the shade of Allah(swt), when no other shade will be available; one of them is the person who gives charity so secretly that his left hand is not aware of what his right hand has given.(See: Sahih Bukhari 660 and Sahih Muslim 1031)\n3. Nafil fast: The fasts of the month of Ramadan are obligatory. But the other fasts which are ‘Nafil’ namely the three fasts every month (the 13th, 14th and 15th days of the lunar months) also have great importance. It is narrated by Abu-Hurairah:\n“My friend (Muhammad(saws)) directed me never to stop fasting on these three days.”(Sahih Bukhari, 1178 and Sahih Muslim, 721)\n4. It is obligatory for a person who can afford to do so to perform the Hajj once. If he performs it more than once, then it is ‘Nafil’ hajj. Whether the hajj is ‘Wajib’ or ‘Nafil’, it is narrated in the sahih hadith:\nWhoever performs Hajj and stays away from lewdness, wrangling, and obscenities will return home like a newborn.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1521 and Sahih Muslim, 1350)\nWhen a person performs the circumambulation of the Holy Kaaba, for every step that he takes a sin is wiped off and a good deed is written in his favour and his status is raised. (Ibn Khuzaima 2752 and Ibn Hibbaan 3689)\nIn the same way, in other everyday matters also ‘Nafil’ has great importance and entails great rewards. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Whoever relieves a difficulty from a Muslim, Allah(swt) will relieve his difficulty on the Day of Resurrection, whoever hides the faults of a Muslim, Allah(swt) will hide his faults on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah(swt) helps His slave till the slave helps his brother.” (Sahih Muslim, 2699)\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Allah(swt) will show mercy to the one who is lenient in his buying, selling and demanding back his money.” (Sahih Bukhari, 2076)\nThat is, being honest while buying and selling and being soft while demanding back one’s money is also a ‘Nafil’ pious deed. We come to know from this that the doors for nafil deeds are always open. After fulfilling our obligatory acts, depending on our physical and financial condition, we should strive to perform as many nafil pious deeds as possible as these entail great rewards in the Hereafter as narrated in the sahih hadith."],[238,"§Namaz\nIn Arabic, namaz is called ‘salah’. In the Holy Quran, the word ‘salah’ has been used to express various meanings. Some of the important meanings are described below:\n1. One is the special form of worship which is called ‘namaz’. In the Holy Quran wherever the command to establish salah and give zakat occurs, the meaning is ‘namaz’. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَيُقِيمُونَ الصَّلَاةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنَاهُمْ يُنفِقُونَ ٣﴾\nWho believe in the unseen, establish prayer, and spend out of what We have provided for them.\n[Al-Baqara: 3]\nSalah (namaz) is the form of worship which has been mentioned the maximum number of times and it is offered five times every day at designated times:\nإِنَّ الصَّلَاةَ كَانَتْ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ كِتَابًا مَّوْقُوتًا\nIndeed, prayer has been decreed upon the believers a decree of specified times.\n[An-Nisa: 103]\nThe most important thing about ‘namaz’ as compared to the other forms of worship is that while the commandments about the other forms were conveyed to the Holy Prophet(saws) through divine revelations by Jibrail(as), the command for namaz was given by Allah(swt) Himself to the Holy Prophet(saws) on the night of ‘Meraj’ when no third person was present. This has been described in detail in the Sahih Bukhari and Sahih Muslim. (See Sahih Bukhari 349 and Sahih Muslim, 163)\n(For more information see Surah –‘Isra’ of the Holy Quran)\nExcept in the case of namaz, specific conditions have been laid down for other forms of worship. For example, zakat is to be given only if the wealth exceeds a certain amount. Hajj needs to be performed only if a person has the financial ability to do it; in case he does not have the required means, he need not perform it. But in the case of namaz, every man and woman has to offer it irrespective of the state he or she is in so that one remembers Allah(swt) constantly, be it dawn, noon or night.\nActually namaz is the only difference between a Muslim and a kafir (non-Muslim) as is narrated in the sahih hadith:\nThe difference between a man(Muslim) and shirk and kufr is the abandoning of salah. (Sahih Muslim, 82)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“The distinction between them and us is salah. So whoever has abandoned the salah has become a disbeliever.”\n(Tirmizi, 2621; Nasai, 464; Ibn-Maaja)\n“It is narrated by Abu-Huraira that the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) did not consider the abandoning of any act Kufr except the abandoning of namaz.”\n(Haakim, 1:70 and Tirmizi 2622)\nTirmizi does not mention the name of Abu-Huraira but Haakim does.\nFrom these hadith we come to know the great importance of namaz which differentiates a Muslim from a disbeliever because a Muslim is one who obeys the commands of Allah(swt) and namaz is a beautiful way of remembering Allah(swt) and His commands five times every day. And a person who remembers Allah(swt) five times everyday cannot possibly disobey Him nor be unaware of Him. The Holy Quran says in this regard:\nإِنَّ الصَّلَاةَ تَنْهَىٰ عَنِ الْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ ۗ وَلَذِكْرُ اللَّهِ أَكْبَرُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَصْنَعُونَ\nIndeed, prayer prohibits immorality and wrongdoing, and the remembrance of Allah is greater. And Allah knows that which you do.\n[Al-Ankaboot: 45]\nThat is, even after offering salah if you cannot refrain from evil deeds, then Allah(swt) is aware of all that you do.\nIn no other religion has the meaning of worship been explained so clearly. It depends on the worshipper to make the optimum use of salah and get the maximum benefit out of it. Warning the believers, Allah(swt) says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَّبِعُوا خُطُوَاتِ الشَّيْطَانِ ۚ وَمَن يَتَّبِعْ خُطُوَاتِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَإِنَّهُ يَأْمُرُ بِالْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ\nO you who have believed, do not follow the footsteps of Satan. And whoever follows the footsteps of Satan - indeed, he enjoins immorality and wrongdoing.\n[An-Nur: 21]\nOffering salah has many spiritual benefits. A few important ones are being highlighted here:\nSalah is a sign of the success of man. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿قَدْ أَفْلَحَ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ ١ الَّذِينَ هُمْ فِي صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُونَ ٢﴾\nCertainly will the believers have succeeded: They who are during their prayer humbly submissive.\n[Al-Mu’minun: 1, 2]\nThat is, he who fears Allah(swt) offers salah in such a way that Allah(swt) is watching him as indeed He(swt) is. In that case he prays whole-heartedly with his body and soul and as such no other thought can enter his mind other than Allah(swt).\nIt has been commanded to seek the help of Allah(swt) through salah:\n﴿وَاسْتَعِينُوا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلَاةِ ۚ وَإِنَّهَا لَكَبِيرَةٌ إِلَّا عَلَى الْخَاشِعِينَ ٤٥﴾\nAnd seek help through patience and prayer, and indeed, it is difficult except for the humbly submissive [to Allah].\n[Al-Baqara: 45]\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اسْتَعِينُوا بِالصَّبْرِ وَالصَّلَاةِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ ١٥٣﴾\nO you who have believed, seek help through patience and prayer. Indeed, Allah is with the patient.\n[Al-Baqara: 153]\nSalah brings a person closer to his God. And as such his heart becomes full of the remembrance of Allah(swt) and such a person does not care about the pains and troubles of this world. In this context the Holy Quran says:\n﴿أَلَا إِنَّ أَوْلِيَاءَ اللَّـهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ ٦٢﴾\nUnquestionably, [for] the allies of Allah there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve.\n[Yunus: 62]\nNamaz is that form of worship about which the Holy Prophet(saws) has said:\nThe comfort and delight of my eyes has been placed in salah. (Musnad Ahmad, 3:128)\nThe Holy Prophet’s(saws) way of offering the salah:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said:\nPerform salah as you see me perform salah.\n(Sahih Bukhari, 631 and Sahih Muslim, 674)\nHow did the Holy Prophet(saws) offer salah? Let us study this:\nFor seventeen months in Madina, the Holy Prophet(saws) prayed facing the Baitul-Muqaddas. But it was his wish that the Holy Kaaba be made the qibla. Then this verse was revealed:\nقَدْ نَرَىٰ تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّمَاءِ ۖ فَلَنُوَلِّيَنَّكَ قِبْلَةً تَرْضَاهَا ۚ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ ۚ وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ\nWe have certainly seen the turning of your face, [O Muhammad], toward the heaven, and We will surely turn you to a qiblah with which you will be pleased. So turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram. And wherever you [believers] are, turn your faces toward it [in prayer].\n[Al-Baqara: 144]\nAfter turning one’s face towards the Holy Kaaba, raise both the hands till the shoulders and then fold them over the chest in such a way that the right hand is over the left hand. (See: Sahih Ibn-Khuzaima, 479)\nThen recite the dua-e-Istifatah (that is the supplication for the beginning of the namaz). One of them is:\n“Allahumma, ba'id baini wa baina khatayaya kama ba'adta baina-l-mashriqi wa-l-maghrib. Allahumma, naqqim min khatayaya kama yunaqqa-ththawbu-l-abyadu mina-ddanas. Allahumma, ighsil khatayaya bil-ma'i wa-th-thalji wal-barad (O Allah! Set me apart from my sins (faults) as the East and West are set apart from each other and clean me from sins as a white garment is cleaned of dirt (after thorough washing). O Allah! Wash off my sins with water, snow and hail.)\"\nOne supplication narrated by Ali(ra) can also be recited. One other supplication mentioned by Umar(ra) which goes as follows can also be recited:\n“Subhanakallahumma wa bihamdika, wa tabarrakasmuka, wa ta'ala jadduka, wa la ilaha ghayruk.” (You are glorified O Allah and praised! Your Name is Blessed; Your Majesty is Exalted and none has the right to be worshipped save You.)\nThen recite surah Fatiha. Namaz offered without surah Fatiha is incomplete.(Sahih Bukhari, 756 and Sahih Muslim, 394)\nAfter this any surah from the Holy Quran can be recited.\nThen saying Allah-u-Akbar raise both hands till the shoulders and bend with both hands on the knees (ruku) and stay in this position calmly. (Sahih Bukhari, 707)\n“Subhanakallahumma rabbana wa bi hamdika, Allahumma-ghfir li (Glory is to you, O Allah, and to You is praise. O Allah, forgive me.)” (Sahih Bukhari, 4968 and Sahih Muslim, 484)\nOr the following supplication can be recited:\n“Subhana Rabbiyal Adheem (Glory be to my Mighty Lord)”\n(Sahih Muslim, 772)\nThen saying “Sami-Allahu liman hamidah” raise both the hands till the shoulders and stand straight and recite the following supplication:\n\"Allahumma Rabbana lakal-hamdu mil'assamawati wal-ardi, wa mil'a ma shi'ta min shai'in ba'du, ahlaththana'i wal majdi,ahaqqu ma qal-al'abdu, wa kulluna laka 'abdun. Allahumma la mani'a lima a'taita, wa la mu'tiya lima man'ata, wa la yanfa'u dhal-jaddi minka--ljaddu (O Allah, our Rabb (Lord), to You is praise in all the heavens and all the earth, and all that pleases You to create afterwards, O You, Who are worthy of praise and glory, most worthy of what a slave says, and we are all Your slaves, no one can withhold what You give, or give what You withhold, and riches cannot avail a wealthy person against You.\"\n(Sahih Muslim, 478)\nThen say “Allah-u-Akbar” and with the utmost concentration and humility prostrate. Prostration should be such that the fingers of both the hands should be pointing towards the qibla and the arms should be away from the body and the space should be such that a small animal like a cat can pass through it. (Sahih Muslim, 497)\nSeven parts of the body should be touching the ground during prostration: forehead, both the hands, both the knees and both the feet.(Sahih Muslim, 491) and recite the following supplication during the prostration:\n“Subhana Rabbiyal-Aala” (Glory is to my Lord the most High). (Sahih Muslim, 772)\nOr recite the following supplication:\n\"Allahumma ghfirli dhambi qullah diqqahu wa jillah wa awwalahu wa akhirahu wa a'la niyatahu wa sirrah\"\n(O Lord, forgive me all my sins, small and great, first and last, open and secret.) (Sahih Muslim, 483)\nThen reciting ‘Allahu-Akbar’ get up from the prostration and calmly remain seated and recite the following supplication:\n“Rabbigh-firli Rabbighfirli”\n(Ibn-Maaja, 897 and Haakim, 1:271)\nThen reciting ‘Allahu-Akbar’ prostrate and recite the supplications mentioned earlier. Other than these if we wish to recite more supplications we can do so.\nThen saying ‘Allahu-Akbar’ get into sitting position. Then calmly put the hands on the ground and get up and fold the hands again with the right hand over the left hand. This completes one ‘rakat’.\nAfter praying the second rakat similarly, be seated in ‘Tashahhud’ such that the left foot is turned right. Put both the hands on the knees with the index finger of the right hand raised up. And recite the following supplication:\n\"At-tahiyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat- taiyibatu assalamu alayka aiyuhannabiyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu. Assalamu alaina wa ala ibadi-Ilahis-salihin. Ashhadu an la ilaha illallahu wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan abduhu wa rasuluhu.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 831 and Sahih Muslim 402)\nThis is the most popular supplication of Abdullah-bin-Masood. Other supplications recited by the other companions are also recorded.\nThen recite Durood Sharif, \"Allah Humma Salle Ala Mohammadiyon Wa Ala Ale Mohammadin Kama Sallaita Aala ibraheema Wa Ala Aalay ibraheema inna Ka Hameedum Majeed. Allah Humma Baarik Aala Mohammadiyon Wa Ala Ale Mohammadin Kama Barakta Ala ibraheema Wa Ala Ale ibraheema inna Ka Hameedum Majeed.\"\nThen any other supplication we wish to recite can be done. Before ending the salat by turning the head to the right and then left, we should seek refuge in Allah(swt) from four things:\n\"Allah humma 'innee a'u'thu bika min athabi jahannam wa min athabil qabri wa min fitnatil mah yaw al mamatee wa min shar-ril masihid-daj-jal”\n[Oh Allah, I seek refuge with You from the punishment of Hellfire, and from the punishment of the grave, and from the trials of living and dying, and from the evil (trials) of the False Christ]\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1377 and Sahih Muslim 588)\nThen turn the head first to the right and then to the left saying “Assalamu-alaikum wa Rahamatullah, Assalamu-alaikum wa Rahamatullah”. This completes two rakats.\nThis was the Holy Prophet(saws)’s way of performing salah as narrated in the sahih hadith by his companions Abu-Huraira, Ibn-Umar, Wa’il-bin-Hajar, Ali, Ubaada-bin-Saamit, Abu-Humaid etc. In fact, Abu-Humaid Saaidi performed namaaz saying that he would show how the Holy Prophet(saws) performed it and offered it in this way in the presence of ten other companions.\n2. The other meaning of ‘salah’ is normal worship performed in any other way. In this regard we may say that the salah performed by the other prophets comes under this category because they must not have offered salah as it was offered by the Holy Prophet(saws). Actually we cannot comment on it because we do not have information about it. Some prophets in whose connection the word ‘salah’ is used in the Holy Quran are :\nIbraheem(as):\nرَبِّ اجْعَلْنِي مُقِيمَ الصَّلَاةِ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِي ۚ\nMy Lord, make me an establisher of prayer, and [many] from my descendants.\n[Ibraheem: 40]\nIsmael(as):\n﴿وَكَانَ يَأْمُرُ أَهْلَهُ بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ وَكَانَ عِندَ رَبِّهِ مَرْضِيًّا ٥٥﴾\nAnd he used to enjoin on his people prayer and zakah and was to his Lord pleasing.\n[Maryam: 55]\nMusa(as):\n﴿إِنَّنِي أَنَا اللَّـهُ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا أَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِي وَأَقِمِ الصَّلَاةَ لِذِكْرِي ١٤﴾\nIndeed, I am Allah. There is no deity except Me, so worship Me and establish prayer for My remembrance.\n[Ta-Ha: 14]\nIsa(as):\n﴿وَجَعَلَنِي مُبَارَكًا أَيْنَ مَا كُنتُ وَأَوْصَانِي بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا ٣١﴾\nAnd He has made me blessed wherever I am and has enjoined upon me prayer and zakah as long as I remain alive.\n[Maryam: 31]\nLuqman also enjoined prayer upon his offspring:\nيَا بُنَيَّ أَقِمِ الصَّلَاةَ وَأْمُرْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَانْهَ عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ وَاصْبِرْ عَلَىٰ مَا أَصَابَكَ\nO my son, establish prayer, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and be patient over what befalls you.\n[Luqman: 17]\nWe also come to know from the Torah that the prophets were commanded to perform ‘salah’. For example: Ibraheem (Genesis, 20:17), Yaqub (Genesis, 32:26-31), Musa (Numbers, 11:2) etc. have been enjoined prayer. But in the translation ‘salah’ has been replaced with ‘worship’.\n3. One other meaning of ‘salah’ is ‘invocation’ as Allah(swt) commanded the Holy Prophet(saws):\nوَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْ ۖ إِنَّ صَلَاتَكَ سَكَنٌ لَّهُمْ\nAnd invoke [Allah 's blessings] upon them. Indeed, your invocations are reassurance for them.\n[At-Tawba: 103]\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“If somebody invites you to a feast, you should accept the invitation. In case you are fasting, then pray for the person inviting you and inform him that you are fasting and hence cannot take part in the feast.In case you are not fasting, take part in the feast.” (Sahih Muslim, 1150)\n4. One meaning of ‘salat’ is to send blessings as it says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ وَمَلَائِكَتَهُ يُصَلُّونَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ ۚ يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا صَلُّوا عَلَيْهِ وَسَلِّمُوا تَسْلِيمًا ٥٦﴾\nIndeed, Allah confers blessing upon the Prophet, and His angels [ask Him to do so]. O you who have believed, ask [Allah to confer] blessing upon him and ask [Allah to grant him] peace. [Al-Ahzab: 56]\nOne meaning of ‘salah’ is the favours of the Almighty(swt). It says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿أُولَـٰئِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ صَلَوَاتٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِمْ وَرَحْمَةٌ ۖ وَأُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُهْتَدُونَ ١٥٧﴾\nThose are the ones upon whom are blessings from their Lord and mercy. And it is those who are the [rightly] guided.\n[Al-Baqara: 157]\n‘Salat’ also means ‘place of worship’. In the Holy Quran four types of places of worship have been mentioned for the four tribes. One is ‘salawat’ which is the place of worship of the Jews:\nوَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ اللَّهِ النَّاسَ بَعْضَهُم بِبَعْضٍ لَّهُدِّمَتْ صَوَامِعُ وَبِيَعٌ وَصَلَوَاتٌ وَمَسَاجِدُ يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا اسْمُ اللَّهِ كَثِيرًا ۗ\nAnd were it not that Allah checks the people, some by means of others, there would have been demolished monasteries, churches, synagogues, and mosques in which the name of Allah is much mentioned.\n[Al-Hajj: 40]\nIn fact, the word ‘salat’ is prominently used to mean ‘namaz’. The compulsory or obligatory salahs are the five daily salahs. Other salahs are described below:\nTahajjud salah:\nThis salah is offered in the third part of the night because at this time Allah(swt) comes down towards the earth.\nThe Messenger of Allah(saw) said:\"Our LORD descends to the lowest heaven during the Last Third of The Night,inquiring, \"Who will call on ME so that I may Respond to Him? Who is asking something of ME so I may Give it to him?,Who is Asking for MY FORGIVENESS so I may FORGIVE HIM..\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1145 and Sahih Muslim, 785)\nThis is the reason the devout offer the Tahajjud salah regularly. The Holy Prophet(saws) was so diligent in offering this salah that his feet would be swollen from standing continuously. When people asked him as to why he prayed so much when Allah(swt) had already forgiven all his past and future sins, he(saws) replied:\n“Should I therefore not be a grateful slave of my Allah(swt)?”\nJumu’a salah:\nSee: ‘Jumu’a’.\nSalahs of the two festivals (Namaz-e-Eidain):\nNamaz-e-Eidain means the salah of the two festivals. One is the Eid-ul-Fitr salah which is prayed after the completion of one month of Ramadan fasts. The second one is the Eid-ul-Azha salah which is offered on the tenth day of the month of Zil-Hijja. On this day, the Haji comes to Mina from Arafat and makes the sacrifice. On Eid-ul-Azha, the sacrifice is done after the salah. This is to commemorate the supreme sacrifice done by Ibraheem(as) when he got ready to sacrifice his only son Ismael(as) following the command of Allah(swt). Allah(swt) was pleased with this action of His slave and sacrificed a sheep instead of Ismael(as) and kept Ismael(as) alive. This incident is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ السَّعْيَ قَالَ يَا بُنَيَّ إِنِّي أَرَىٰ فِي الْمَنَامِ أَنِّي أَذْبَحُكَ فَانظُرْ مَاذَا تَرَىٰ ۚ قَالَ يَا أَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ ۖ سَتَجِدُنِي إِن شَاءَ اللَّـهُ مِنَ الصَّابِرِينَ ١٠٢ فَلَمَّا أَسْلَمَا وَتَلَّهُ لِلْجَبِينِ ١٠٣ وَنَادَيْنَاهُ أَن يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ ١٠٤ قَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّؤْيَا ۚ إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ ١٠٥ إِنَّ هَـٰذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلَاءُ الْمُبِينُ ١٠٦ وَفَدَيْنَاهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيمٍ ١٠٧ وَتَرَكْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِي الْآخِرِينَ ١٠٨ سَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ إِبْرَاهِيمَ ١٠٩ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ ١١٠ إِنَّهُ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ١١١﴾\nAnd when he reached with him [the age of] exertion, he said, \"O my son, indeed I have seen in a dream that I [must] sacrifice you, so see what you think.\" He said, \"O my father, do as you are commanded. You will find me, if Allah wills, of the steadfast.\" And when they had both submitted and he put him down upon his forehead, We called to him, \"O Abraham, You have fulfilled the vision.\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good. Indeed, this was the clear trial. And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice, And We left for him [favorable mention] among later generations: \"Peace upon Abraham.\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good. Indeed, he was of Our believing servants. [As-Saffat: 102-111]\nThus, remembering this beautiful incident Muslims perform the sacrifice every year on Eid-ul-Azha.\nJanaza salah:\nIt is obligatory upon Muslims that when one of them dies, they should perform the Namaz-e-Janaza before burying him. When a few Muslims perform this salah, then the others are free from the obligation. This is termed as ‘Fard-e-Kifaya’ under Islamic law or ‘Fiqh’. But if the salah is not performed for anyone, then the Islamic society as a whole will be the sinner because just as every Muslim has certain rights in a society as long as he lives, even after death he has some rights. For example : giving the funeral bath, covering him with the funeral shroud and praying the namaz-e-janaza for him or her and then burying him or her.\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“The five rights that a Muslim has over another Muslim are:- 1) He must reply to the greetings of Salaam. 2) He should visit him when he is sick. 3) Accompany funeral processions 4) Accept his invitations 5) Respond when he says \"Alhamdulillah\" or something like that when he sneezes by replying with \"`Yarhamuk-Allah\" (may Allah bestow His Mercy on you).\n(Sahih Bukhari, 1240 and Sahih Muslim, 2162)\nNamaz-e-Janaza which is called ‘salat’ in Arabic is in fact a supplication for the dead person. The meaning of one of the most popular supplications is as follows:\n‘O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, those present and those absent, our young and our old, our males and our females. O Allah, whom amongst us You keep alive, then let such a life be upon Islam, and whom amongst us You take unto Yourself, then let such a death be upon faith. O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward and do not let us stray after him.’\n(Abu-Dawood-3201, Tirmizi-1024 and Ibn-Majah-1498)\nSalah in case of fear:\nThe supreme importance of namaz can be understood from the fact that it has been commanded to pray even during war. But the concession has been given that instead of four rakats, only two can be offered. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَإِذَا ضَرَبْتُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَقْصُرُوا مِنَ الصَّلَاةِ إِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَن يَفْتِنَكُمُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ۚ إِنَّ الْكَافِرِينَ كَانُوا لَكُمْ عَدُوًّا مُّبِينًا ١٠١ وَإِذَا كُنتَ فِيهِمْ فَأَقَمْتَ لَهُمُ الصَّلَاةَ فَلْتَقُمْ طَائِفَةٌ مِّنْهُم مَّعَكَ وَلْيَأْخُذُوا أَسْلِحَتَهُمْ فَإِذَا سَجَدُوا فَلْيَكُونُوا مِن وَرَائِكُمْ وَلْتَأْتِ طَائِفَةٌ أُخْرَىٰ لَمْ يُصَلُّوا فَلْيُصَلُّوا مَعَكَ وَلْيَأْخُذُوا حِذْرَهُمْ وَأَسْلِحَتَهُمْ ۗ وَدَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ تَغْفُلُونَ عَنْ أَسْلِحَتِكُمْ وَأَمْتِعَتِكُمْ فَيَمِيلُونَ عَلَيْكُم مَّيْلَةً وَاحِدَةً ۚ وَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِن كَانَ بِكُمْ أَذًى مِّن مَّطَرٍ أَوْ كُنتُم مَّرْضَىٰ أَن تَضَعُوا أَسْلِحَتَكُمْ ۖ وَخُذُوا حِذْرَكُمْ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ أَعَدَّ لِلْكَافِرِينَ عَذَابًا مُّهِينًا ١٠٢﴾\nAnd when you travel throughout the land, there is no blame upon you for shortening the prayer, [especially] if you fear that those who disbelieve may disrupt [or attack] you. Indeed, the disbelievers are ever to you a clear enemy.And when you are among them and lead them in prayer, let a group of them stand [in prayer] with you and let them carry their arms. And when they have prostrated, let them be [in position] behind you and have the other group come forward which has not [yet] prayed and let them pray with you, taking precaution and carrying their arms. Those who disbelieve wish that you would neglect your weapons and your baggage so they could come down upon you in one [single] attack. But there is no blame upon you, if you are troubled by rain or are ill, for putting down your arms, but take precaution. Indeed, Allah has prepared for the disbelievers a humiliating punishment.\n[An-Nisa: 101, 102]\nWe come to know from the sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) offered salah in case of fear in different forms depending on the situation and the type of fear or danger. Therefore, Imam Ahmad is of the opinion that all the different forms of salah are acceptable depending on the situation. The aim is to neither leave the salah nor let the enemy attack. If it is difficult to offer salah with the proper bowing and prostration, then it can also be offered standing or even while mounted on a horse. This clearly means that it is imperative for every Muslim to remember Allah(swt) at all times. Remember Allah(swt) even in the battle-field and seek His help.\nSalah while travelling:\nJust as the namaz can be shortened when a battle is on, it can be shortened even during a journey. One companion named Yaala-bin-Umaiyya questioned Umar-bin-Khattab, “Allah(swt) has commanded us to shorten the namaz in case of fear. But why should we shorten them on a journey when there is no fear?” Umar replied that when he asked the question to the Holy Prophet(saws), he(saws) replied,\n“This is a gift to you from Allah(swt). So, accept the gift.”\n(Sahih Muslim-686)\nThat is, the shortening of salah which is called ‘Qasr’ is to be done in case of fear of danger and as a special concession even while travelling. Most of the scholars are of the opinion that instead of offering the full namaz while travelling, it is better to shorten it.\nOne other concession given when a person is travelling is that two prayers can be combined and offered. That is, the Dhuhr and Asr and the Magrib and Isha salahs can be combined. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that when the Holy Prophet(saws) began his travel before the sun had begun its descent, then he(saws) would delay his Dhuhr salah and when it was time for the Asr salah, he(saws) would offer both of them together. But in case he(saws) began his journey after the sun had begun its descent, that is after the time for the Dhuhr salah had begun, then he(saws) would offer the Dhuhr salah and then immediately offer the Asr salah and then begin his journey. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 1112 and Sahih Muslim, 704)\nIn one other sahih hadith it is narrated that Mu’aaz-bin-Jabal said that when they were starting for the battle of Tabuk, The Holy Prophet(saws) offered the Dhuhr and Asr salahs together and similarly offered the Magrib and Isha salahs together. (See: Sahih Muslim, 706)\nCombining two salahs is for a person who is on a journey so that he is not inconvenienced in any way. But, sometimes it is permissible to combine two salahs even while the person is not travelling if the need arises and it is not a sin. As is narrated by Abdullah-bin-Abbas that the Holy Prophet(saws) combined the Dhuhr and Asr salahs and the Magrib and Isha salahs even when there was no fear nor was he(saws) travelling. (See: Sahih Muslim, 705)\nZuha Salah:\nZuha is the time when we begin to perceive the heat of the sun; that is around 9 or 10 in the morning. Zuha salah is the salah offered sometimes by the Holy Prophet(saws) at around this time varying from two to eight rakats. It is narrated by a hadith of Umme-Haani that after the victory over Makka, the Holy Prophet(saws) came to his house, had a bath and then offered eight rakat namaz which was small but all the rukus and prostrations were done properly. (See: Sahih Bukhari, 1176 and Sahih Muslim, 336)\nWhen Aisha(as) was asked as to how many rakat the Holy Prophet(saws) prayed in the Zuha salah, she replied: four or sometimes more than that. (See: Sahih Muslim, 719)\nIt is narrated in another sahih hadith that a human body has three hundred and sixty joints and it is obligatory to offer charity for every joint. People asked, “O Apostle of Allah, who has so much capacity.” The Holy Prophet(saws) replied that if one cleans the mosque or removes some obstruction from the pathway or if unable to do any of these things, prays two rakat Zuha salah, then his charity is done. (See: Abu Dawood, 5242, Ibn-Khuzaima, 1226) and Ibn-Hibbaan, 2540 whose chain of narrators is hasan.\nNamaz-e-Istisqa:\nIstisqa means to seek water. That is why this salah is offered when there is drought in a place. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) came out to offer the istisqa salah. First he offered two rakat and then turned his outer garment (shawl) around such that the left side is to the right and the right side is to the left. Then he(saws) raised both the hands and prayed for rain. As a result the whole of Madina was flooded with water.\nNamaz-e-Kasoof:\n‘Kasoof’ means ‘eclipse’. Before the advent of Islam, people entertained various superstitions in connection with the solar and lunar eclipses. When Ibraheem, the son of the Holy Prophet(saws) passed away there was a solar eclipse. So, people started saying that it was due to the death of Ibraheem. When the Holy Prophet(saws) came to know about this, he assembled all of them and said that the sun and the moon were the signs of Allah(swt) and the eclipses do not occur due to someone living or dying. That is why whenever there is an eclipse, offer salah and supplicate to Allah(swt). (See: Sahih Bukhari, 1060 and Sahih Muslim, 91)\nNamaz-e-Kasoof doesn’t have any designated number of rakats but keep offering two-two rakats till the eclipse lasts. It is narrated in another sahih hadith that eclipses are the signs of Allah(swt) and therefore whenever there is an eclipse spend the time in the remembrance of Allah(swt), seeking His forgiveness and supplicating to Him(swt).\nNamaz-e-Istikhara:\n‘Istikhara’ means to adopt one way when there are two ways. This salah is offered when someone is facing some problem. A person then prays to Allah(swt) to turn his heart towards whatever is best for him. The method of performing this salah is described in the sahih hadith. Before retiring to bed, after praying the fard namaz, pray two additional rakat and then recite the following supplication:\n'Allahumma inni astakhiruka bi'ilmika, Wa astaqdiruka bi-qudratika, Wa as'alaka min fadlika al-'azlm Fa-innaka taqdiru Wala aqdiru, Wa ta'lamu Wala a'lamu, Wa anta 'allamu l-ghuyub. Allahumma, in kunta ta'lam anna hadha-l-amra Khairun li fi dini wa ma'ashi wa'aqibati amri (or 'ajili amri wa'ajilihi) Faqdirhu wa yas-sirhu li thumma barik li Fihi, Wa in kunta ta'lamu anna hadha-lamra shar-run li fi dini wa ma'ashi wa'aqibati amri (or fi'ajili amri wa ajilihi) Fasrifhu anni was-rifni anhu. Waqdir li al-khaira haithu kana Thumma ardini bihi.’\n(O Allah! I ask guidance from Your knowledge, And Power from Your Might and I ask for Your great blessings. You are capable and I am not. You know and I do not and You know the unseen. O Allah! If You know that this job is good for my religion and my subsistence and in my Hereafter--(or said: If it is better for my present and later needs)--Then You ordain it for me and make it easy for me to get, And then bless me in it, and if You know that this job is harmful to me In my religion and subsistence and in the Hereafter--(or said: If it is worse for my present and later needs)--Then keep it away from me and let me be away from it. And ordain for me whatever is good for me, And make me satisfied with it)\nThe Prophet (sal-allahu-alleihi-wasallam) added that then the person should name (mention) his need.\"\n(See: Sahih Bukhari, 1162)\nAs a result of this namaz, the correct solution for his problem will emerge and Allah(swt) will make him content with what is best for him.\nNamaz-e-Tasbeeh:\nThis is a type of salah which has been described in some hadith, but none of the sanads(chain of narrators) is reliable. It is narrated that the Holy Prophet(saws) told his paternal uncle Abbas, “If possible offer this salah every day, or if not possible offer it once a week. If that is difficult, then offer it once a month. If that is not possible, then offer it once a year. If even that is not possible, then offer it at least once in a lifetime.”\nNamaz-e-Ragaib:\nScholars are of the opinion that this namaz became popular in the fourth century A.H and hence the offering of this salah is ‘biddat’.\nNamaz-e-Haaja:\nThis is the salah offered for the fulfillment of some need. I have come across three hadith in this regard and all of them are ‘Zaeef Jiddan’. Therefore the namaz offered as ‘namaz-e-haaja’ does not have any confirmation in any sahih hadith."],[239,"§Name\nRegarding the naming of a person and then calling him by that name, Islam has two important instructions:\nBefore the advent of Islam, when someone adopted a child, then the child was known by the name of the person who had adopted him. That is why when the Holy Prophet(saws) adopted Zaid-bin-Haritha, then people started calling him Zaid-bin-Muhammad. The Holy Quran categorically condemns it:\nادْعُوهُمْ لِآبَائِهِمْ هُوَ أَقْسَطُ عِندَ اللَّهِ\nCall them by [the names of] their fathers; it is more just in the sight of Allah.\n[Al-Ahzab: 5]\nThat is why no adopted son is called by the name of his adopted father, nor will he be considered his real father. That is, the various laws and commandments regarding the biological father and son will not be applicable in the case of the father and his adopted son. For example in case of Meeras, marriage etc.\nWe also understand from this that it is best to suffix the name of the father to the son’s name instead of one person having two or three names. For example if someone is named ‘Ahmad Muhammad Abdullah’, then it is not right because nowhere is it mentioned that any sahabi or Imam or muhaddis(scholar of hadith) or ordinary person for that matter had two or three names in the days of the Holy Prophet(saws). But this practice is prevalent in many countries due to which the Arabs find it difficult to understand if it is the name of one person or two or three persons or if the names are those of his father and grandfather. It is narrated in a sahih hadith that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\n\"I have five names. I am Muhammad. I am Ahmad. I am al-Mahi (the effacer), by whom Allah effaces kufr. I am al-Hashir (the gatherer), before whom people are gathered. I am al-Aqib (the last).\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 3532 and Sahih Muslim, 2354)\nThese noble names of the Holy Prophet(saws) are to describe his qualities. It is narrated in another sahih hadith:\n“I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am Mukhaffa, I am Nabiyyut-tauba, I am Nabiyyul-Malahim.” (Sahih Muslim, 2355)\nThat is why some scholars have attributed more than twenty names to the Holy Prophet(saws).But his actual name was just one, Muhammad-bin-Abdullah. In the same way it is improper to suffix the name of the husband to the wife’s name after marriage. For example Zainab becomes Zainab Fareed after marriage because Fareed is the name of the husband. This goes against the following verse of the Holy Quran:\nادْعُوهُمْ لِآبَائِهِمْ هُوَ أَقْسَطُ عِندَ اللَّهِ\nCall them by [the names of] their fathers.\n[Al-Ahzab: 5]\nIslam recognizes the rights of women and accords them respect. That is why whether she is married or unmarried, she is to be addressed by her own name. She is either called Zainab Abdullah that is, Zainab the daughter of Abdullah or Zainab the wife of Fareed. It is important to mention the word wife here so that she is not considered the daughter of Fareed. This goes against the modern custom which does not treat women with respect. Before marriage she is called Miss George and after marriage she becomes Mrs. John.The question arises as to what is her individuality? Does not this go against the rights and respect of a woman?\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“On the Day of Resurrection you will be called by your own name and the names of your fathers. So, select good names.”\n(Abu-Dawood, 4948; Musnad Ahmad, 5:194)\nThe second instruction regarding names is that good names must be selected for one’s children.It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Allah(swt) likes the names Abdullah and Abdur-Rehman the most.” (Sahih Muslim, 2132)\nThat is, the names which mean that the person is a slave of Allah(swt). For example Abdul-Kareem (slave of Kareem), Abdur-Raheem (slave of Raheem), Abdul-Azeem (slave of Azeem), Abdul-Jabbar (slave of Jabbar) etc. because all these are the names of Allah(swt). After these the preferred names are the names of the prophets: Muhammad(saws), Ahmad, Adam, Nuh, Ibraheem, Ismael, Ishaq, Yaqub, Yusuf, Sulaiman, Musa, Haroon, Isa etc.\nAfter these the preferred names are those of the companions: Abu Bakr, Umar, Usman, Ali, Zubair, Ubaida, Hasan, Hussain etc.\nAfter these the preferred names are those which have a beautiful meaning: Aadil, Faisal, Fahad, Shafeeq, Sahal, Suhail, Saeed etc.\nThe names of the angels can also be selected: Jibrail, Michael, Israfeel etc. As the angels also have been created by Allah(swt) it is allowed to adopt their names. But some scholars think otherwise.\n“The worst name in the sight of Allah(swt) is when a person is named Malikul-Mulk( King of Kings).”\n(Sahih Bukhari 6205 and Sahih Muslim 2143)\nIn the same way we need to refrain from selecting names which praise oneself. For example Barrah, which means someone who is very pious.\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that the original name of Zainab was ‘Barrah’ and the Holy Prophet(saws) changed it to Zainab. (Sahih Bukhari, 6192 and Sahih Muslim, 2141)\nIn the same way, names which had a bad meaning were disliked by the Holy Prophet(saws).\nIt is narrated in a sahih hadith that a person came to the Holy Prophet(saws) and he(saws) asked him his name. The man replied, ‘Huzan’ which means ‘difficulty’ or ‘grief’. The Holy Prophet(saws) said, “You are not ‘Huzan’ but ‘Sahal’. The man replied, “I will not change the name given by my people.” The Holy Prophet(saws) kept quiet.\nIn the same way the names which are not preferred are Pharaoh(Firaun), Qaroon, Haman etc., upon whom was the wrath of Allah(swt).\nThe names in which a person is described as a slave of someone other than Allah(swt) are also not to be selected. For example: Abdun-Nabi, Abdur-Rasool etc. As the meaning of ‘Abd’ is slave, it is also not proper to select names like Ghulam Muhammad, Ghulam Rasool etc.\nThese rules while naming the children apply to both girls and boys. Even while naming the girls we need to bear it in mind that the names are not only pleasant with beautiful meaning but that they do not in any way mean that the person is a slave of someone other than Allah(swt)."],[240,"§Narrator\nNarrator or ‘Ravi’ is a person who narrates a hadith. Only after analyzing these narrators is a hadith declared ‘Sahih’ or ‘Zaeef’ because it has been instructed in Surah Al-Hujurat, Verse-6 that if a disobedient person comes to you with some information then investigate it thoroughly. Before declaring a hadith as ‘Sahih’ or ‘Zaeef’, many things need to be kept in mind; but the foremost and compulsory requisite is that all the narrators have to be truthful. A hadith narrated by an untruthful narrator can never be truthful. There are various degrees of truthfulness of the narrators which the great hadith scholar Hafiz Ibn-Hajar(expired 852 A.H) has classified into eight levels. This has been mentioned here to give an idea of the hard work which goes into the research of the hadith.\nThe twelve levels of the narrators:\nFirst level:\nIf it is proved that the narrator was a companion of the Holy Prophet(saws) then we need not research about that narrator as we can safely believe that all companions were truthful as is confirmed in the Holy Quran and the sahih hadith.\nSecond level:\nFor the narrators in this category the word best is used; that is, the narrator is not only truthful but his memory is also excellent. For these narrators, it is said that he is a very truthful narrator or that he is truthful, truthful.\nThird level:\nThe narrator in this category is truthful but his memory is a little weak. For them, only one word is used; like, he is truthful, he remembers, is alright etc.\nFourth level:\nIn this category the narrator’s memory is less than that of the narrator of the previous category. The word ‘Sadooq’ is used or it is said that ‘there is no objection.’\nFifth level:\nIn this category, the memory of the narrator is weaker than the memory of the narrator of the previous category. So, in addition to the word ‘Sadooq’ it is said that the memory of the narrator is weak. Or he may have been misled in narrating a hadith. Or in the end he may have been led astray or leaving the truthful instructions he had started doing ‘biddat’ or innovations in religion.\nSixth level:\nIn this category the narrator is such that he has very few hadith but no information is available about him so as to leave the hadith narrated by him. The word ‘Maqbool’ is used for him which means that his hadith can be accepted as reliable only if the same thing is narrated by some other reliable narrator. If not then the narrator cannot be believed. And the hadith will be between ‘Sahih’ and ‘Zaeef’. Only a hadith scholar can decide this. The hadith narrated by these six categories of narrators can be accepted. The hadith narrated by the narrators of the first three categories will be ‘Sahih’ and those narrated by the narrators of the remaining three categories will be ‘Hasan’.\nThe hadith narrated by the narrators of the remaining six categories will be ‘Zaeef’. Even the ‘Zaeef’ hadith have levels like Zaeef, Zaeef Jiddan, Mauzoo, Munkar etc.\nIn this way, only after a deep and profound research of the narrators can a verdict be passed about them. This is a very difficult task but in every age, Allah(swt) creates hadith scholars who are extremely capable of this difficult task. An incident is mentioned here which gives us an indication of the character of these narrators.\nKhalifa Haroon Rasheed one day issued an order to kill a heretic. The man questioned the Khalifa, “O Ameerul Momineen! Why did you order my killing? The Khalifa replied, “To protect the slaves of Allah(swt) from your evil deeds.” The man replied, “How can you save them when I have fabricated one thousand hadith and spread them among the people?” The Khalifa said, “O enemy of Allah(swt)! How can you compete against the hadith scholars like Abu Ishaq Fijari and Abdullah-bin-Mubarak who clean each and every letter by passing it through a sieve.”( See: Taariq Damishk, 7:127)\nThat is, the fabricated hadith will be clearly indicated as being ‘Mauzoo.’ It has been mentioned that the number of narrators is about five lakh and to study their life three types of books have been written:\n1.The books written about the truthful narrators. For example: Assikhat.\nAuthor: Ijli (Expired: 261 A.H)\nAssikhat, Author: Ibn-Hibban (Expired: 354 A.H)\nAssikhat, Author: Ibn-Shaheen (385 A.H)\n2.The books written about ‘Zaeef’ narrators:\nZuafae-Kabir, Author: Bukhari (Expired 256 A.H)\nAhwale Rijaal, Author: Zojjaani (Expired 259 A.H)\nZuafa wa Matrookeen, Author: Nasai (Expired 303 A.H)\nZuafae-Kabir, Author: Ukhaili (Expired 322 A.H)\nMaarifatul-Majrooheen, Author: Ibn-Hibbaan (Expired: 354 A.H)\nAlkaamil Fi Zuafa, Author: Ibn-Adi (Expired: 365 A.H)\n3.The books about the truthful and the weak narrators:\nTabqaat Kubra, Author: Ibn-Saad (Expired: 230 A.H)\nTaareeq Kabir, Author: Bukhari (Expired: 256 A.H)\nTaareeq Kabir, Author: Ibn-Abi Khaisma (Expired: 279 A.H)\nJarah wa taadeel, Author: Ibn-Abi-Haatim (Expired: 327 A.H)\nTahzeebul-kamaal Fi-Asmaur-rijal, Author: Jamaluddin Mizzi (Expired 752 A.H)\nThis book has the biographies of more than eight thousand people and has been published in thirty volumes.\nTahzeebut-tahzeeb, Author: Hafiz Ibn-Hajar (Expired: 852 A.H)\nThis is actually the concise version of the book of Mizzi which has been published in twelve volumes.\nIn this the author has included his own views also and because Ibn-Hajar is a great scholar of hadith, his opinions are very important.\nTaqreebut-tahzeeb, Author: Hafiz Ibn-Hajar (Expired 852 A.H)\nThis is a gist of Tahzeebut-tahzeeb in which the author has described in just one or two words, the level of the narrator as a result of which the task of the people who research the hadith has become very easy. Other than these several other books have been written about the life histories of the narrators of hadith. The following are the popular books named after a country or city: Taariq-e-Baghdad, Taariq-e-Isfahan, Tariq-e-Neshapur, Tariq-e-Damisk, Tariq-e-Misr, Tariq-e-Hind wa Sind.\nScholars who research the narrators:\nThe number of the scholars who research the narrators are about five hundred and books have been written about their commentaries. The following are the prominent ones:\nAuzai (Expired 158 A.H), Shoba (Expired 160 A.H), Sauri (Expired 101 A.H), Malik (Expired 179 A.H), Ibn-Mubarak (Expired 181 A.H), Ibn-Uaina (Expired 197 A.H),\nYahya Khattaan (Expired 198 A.H), Yahya-Ibn-Muin (Expired 233 A.H), Ahmad-bin-Hambal (Expired: 241 A.H), Bukhari (Expired: 256 A.H), Muslim (Expired: 261 A.H), Abu-Zur’a (Expired: 264 A.H), Abu Hatim (Expired: 277 A.H), Nasai (Expired: 303 A.H), Ukhaili (Expired 322 A.H), Darkhutni (Expired: 385 A.H) etc. In fact the science of hadith is a vast one."],[241,"§Nasara\n‘Nasara’ is the plural of ‘Nasrani’. The word ‘nasara’ has been used for the disciples of Isa(as) in the Holy Quran. The story goes as follows. When Isa(as) was born in Bethlehem (which is to the north of Jerusalem), his mother took him away to Egypt. This was because the king of Jerusalem Herodes came to know that the Messiah who would end his reign was born. As he did not know who the Messiah was, he ordered the killing of all the new-borns.\nAfter the death of Herodes, Maryam came back with Isa(as) to Palestine and instead of Bethlehem settled in a place called ‘Nasira’. According to Matthew, they went and settled in a place called ‘Nazareth’ so that the prophecy of the prophets would be fulfilled that the Messiah would be a ‘Nazarene’.(Bible, Matthew 2:23)\nThe followers of Isa(as) sometimes call themselves brothers, sometimes disciples and sometimes believers; but the Jews call them Nasari or Gulaili and the Christians hate the word.\nThen when St. Peter built the church in Antakya in 43 A.D, he named it ‘Maseeh’.\nWe understand from this that the name used for Maseeh in the Bible is ‘Maseek Nasiri’. That is why his followers were called ‘Nasara’ or ‘Nasrani’. And this is the name which has been used for them in the Holy Quran. But just as there were changes in the teachings of Maseeh(as), there must have been a change in the name used by Maseeh(as) for his disciples. And the later generations have made it ‘Masihi’ which was not used by Maseeh(as).\nIn the Holy Quran, Allah(swt) has explained to the Nasara(Christians) in many places that the teachings of Isa(as) are nothing but what the Holy Quran instructs. On the other hand, Allah(swt) also tells the Muslims that these Nasara are the closest in friendship to you and the Jews are the closest to you in enmity. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿لَتَجِدَنَّ أَشَدَّ النَّاسِ عَدَاوَةً لِّلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا الْيَهُودَ وَالَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا ۖ وَلَتَجِدَنَّ أَقْرَبَهُم مَّوَدَّةً لِّلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّا نَصَارَىٰ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّ مِنْهُمْ قِسِّيسِينَ وَرُهْبَانًا وَأَنَّهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ ٨٢﴾\nYou will surely find the most intense of the people in animosity toward the believers [to be] the Jews and those who associate others with Allah; and you will find the nearest of them in affection to the believers those who say, \"We are Christians.\" That is because among them are priests and monks and because they are not arrogant.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 82]"],[242,"§Nasq\n‘Nasq’ is an Arabic word. It means ‘to erase’. The Holy Quran is the book of Allah(swt). Therefore Allah(swt) has the right to either ‘Nasq’ a portion of it or let it remain. Nobody has a right to comment on this. And Allah(swt) has laid down a rule for this:\n﴿مَا نَنسَخْ مِنْ آيَةٍ أَوْ نُنسِهَا نَأْتِ بِخَيْرٍ مِّنْهَا أَوْ مِثْلِهَا ۗ أَلَمْ تَعْلَمْ أَنَّ اللَّـهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ١٠٦﴾\nWe do not abrogate a verse or cause it to be forgotten except that We bring forth [one] better than it or similar to it. Do you not know that Allah is over all things competent?\n[Al-Baqara: 106]\nTwo things have been explained in this verse.\nOne is that when Allah(swt) abrogates a verse, then He(swt) reveals a better one in its place. This does not mean that the previous verse was not good because all the verses of Allah(swt) are nothing but good. It simply means that the new verse is better or easier for the people. As an example let us take the following verse:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ حَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَى الْقِتَالِ ۚ إِن يَكُن مِّنكُمْ عِشْرُونَ صَابِرُونَ يَغْلِبُوا مِائَتَيْنِ ۚ وَإِن يَكُن مِّنكُم مِّائَةٌ يَغْلِبُوا أَلْفًا مِّنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُونَ ٦٥﴾\nO Prophet, urge the believers to battle. If there are among you twenty [who are] steadfast, they will overcome two hundred. And if there are among you one hundred [who are] steadfast, they will overcome a thousand of those who have disbelieved because they are a people who do not understand.\n[Al-Anfal: 65]\nIn the light of this verse we understand that even if the strength of the enemy soldiers is ten times that of the Muslims and the Holy Prophet(saws) gives a call for ‘jihad’, it is the duty of the Muslims to go forth.\nThen, this was repealed and it was made obligatory for a Muslim to go forth for ‘jihad’ when the ruler gave a call only if the strength of the enemy is double that of the Muslim army and not otherwise:\n﴿الْآنَ خَفَّفَ اللَّـهُ عَنكُمْ وَعَلِمَ أَنَّ فِيكُمْ ضَعْفًا ۚ فَإِن يَكُن مِّنكُم مِّائَةٌ صَابِرَةٌ يَغْلِبُوا مِائَتَيْنِ ۚ وَإِن يَكُن مِّنكُمْ أَلْفٌ يَغْلِبُوا أَلْفَيْنِ بِإِذْنِ اللَّـهِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ ٦٦﴾\nNow, Allah has lightened [the hardship] for you, and He knows that among you is weakness. So if there are from you one hundred [who are] steadfast, they will overcome two hundred. And if there are among you a thousand, they will overcome two thousand by permission of Allah. And Allah is with the steadfast.\n[Al-Anfal: 66]\nIn the above verse, when the Muslims are urged to fight, it should not be misunderstood that Islam teaches us to just fight, kill and be killed. These verses were in fact revealed when the disbelievers had made life hell for the believers.\nIn fact, Islam makes every effort to establish a peaceful society. But when the enemies of peace and mischief-makers are bent on ruining the very fabric of society and will not listen to the voice of reason, then it becomes imperative to take up arms against them. But the Holy Quran says that if they incline towards peace, then you too do the same. From this we understand that fighting is not an end in itself but a means of establishing peace. This is the reason why during the ten years of the Holy Prophet(saws)’s stay in Madina, peace was established in the whole of Arabia. The tribes which were engaged in fighting previously became brothers. And during the wars altogether less than a thousand people were killed.\nLet us now come back to the word ‘Nasq’. So, in Surah-2, Verse-106, when it is said that Allah(swt) causes some verses to be forgotten, it could also mean that people had forgotten the divine books revealed before the Holy Quran or caused them to be corrupted with their own views. So, Allah(swt) has caused the previous revelations to be repealed and replaced them with the best book – The Holy Quran. So, the instructions and commandments of all the other books stand annulled except for those which have been retained in the Holy Quran."],[243,"§Nasr\n‘Nasr’ was an idol of the tribe Himyar. For more information see ‘Wadd’."],[244,"§Nazr(vow)\n‘Nazr’ means to make a ‘vow’ to do something if some wish is fulfilled. It is making something obligatory upon oneself which Allah(swt) and the Holy Prophet(saws) have not made obligatory.\nTherefore making a vow for something has not been included among the pious deeds. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\nThe Prophet discouraged the making of ‘nadhar’ (vows) and said, \"It (a vow) does not prevent anything (that has to take place), but (through the vow) the property of a miser is spent (taken out) with it.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 6692 and Sahih Muslim, 1639)\nBut if some vow or ‘Nazr’ has been taken then it should be fulfilled because it is a type of ‘promise’ and if some promise is given then it should be fulfilled.\nThat is why praising those who fulfill their ‘Nazr’, Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿يُوفُونَ بِالنَّذْرِ وَيَخَافُونَ يَوْمًا كَانَ شَرُّهُ مُسْتَطِيرًا ٧﴾\nThey [are those who] fulfill [their] vows and fear a Day whose evil will be widespread.\n[Al-Insan: 7]\nوَمَا أَنفَقْتُم مِّن نَّفَقَةٍ أَوْ نَذَرْتُم مِّن نَّذْرٍ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُهُ\nAnd whatever you spend of expenditures or make of vows - indeed, Allah knows of it.\n[Al-Baqara: 270]\nThat is, fulfill your vows. The command to fulfill one’s vows is given in one other place:\n﴿ثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ وَلْيُوفُوا نُذُورَهُمْ وَلْيَطَّوَّفُوا بِالْبَيْتِ الْعَتِيقِ ٢٩﴾\nThen let them end their untidiness and fulfill their vows and perform Tawaf around the ancient House.\n[Al-Hajj: 29]\nThat is, on the tenth day of Zil-Hijja, after the Haji stones the Jamarah, then he should shave or trim his hair, have a bath and wear stitched clothes and apply perfume. In this way he should clean himself of the grime and dust of the days of Ihram and then fulfill any vows he may have taken. For example if somebody has taken a vow that he will sacrifice ten camels if Allah(swt) helps him complete his Hajj, then he should do so at this time.’Nazr’ should not be made in anyone else’s name other than Allah(swt) as it amounts to ‘shirk’.(See : Surah-31, Luqman, Verse-13)\nIf someone makes a ‘nazr’ which is haraam or unlawful, then it is not compulsory to fulfill it. In fact care should be taken not to fulfill it.\nFor example if someone makes a ‘nazr’ that if Allah(swt) blesses him with a child then he will treat people with wine, or if some work of his gets done then he will donate a ‘chadar’ or ‘shawl’ at some grave or maybe feed people in the name of the wali buried in the dargah etc. Both making and fulfilling these sort of vows or ‘nazr’ are haraam or ‘unlawful’ and ‘shirk’. It is narrated in a sahih hadith:\n“Anyone who promises to obey Allah, he should obey Him. & anyone who promises disobedience to Allah he should not disobey Him”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 6696)\nThat is, do not fulfill the types of vows which have been explained above."],[245,"§Nifaq\n‘Nifaq’ is derived from the Arabic word ‘Nafaq’ which means ‘to pass through’. That is why ‘nafaq’ is also used for a tunnel because you enter it at one end and pass through to the other side. In Islamic terminology, ‘Nifaq’ means to enter the religion through one entrance and come out of the other; that is, to verbally accept Islam but have enmity towards it in the heart.\n‘Nifaq’ is one of the specifically described topics in the Holy Quran. When Islam started spreading rapidly, it became difficult for the disbelievers to combat the onslaught. So, a few of them in order to harm the true religion started verbally accepting Islam but in their heart of hearts the hatred towards the true path and Islam was as strong as ever. And in the guise of Muslims, it became very easy for them to harm the cause of Islam. Therefore these people were called ‘Munafiq’ or ‘hypocrites’. Whatever is said about these hypocrites in the Holy Quran has been mentioned below:\n1.They try to deceive Allah(swt) when they should be well aware that none can deceive Allah(swt). They are the ones who are deceiving themselves.\n﴿يُخَادِعُونَ اللَّـهَ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَمَا يَخْدَعُونَ إِلَّا أَنفُسَهُمْ وَمَا يَشْعُرُونَ ٩﴾\nThey [think to] deceive Allah and those who believe, but they deceive not except themselves and perceive [it] not.\n[Al-Baqara: 9]\n2.They are very lazy in offering their salah and even if they do so, they do it just to make a show of it to the people.\n﴿إِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ يُخَادِعُونَ اللَّـهَ وَهُوَ خَادِعُهُمْ وَإِذَا قَامُوا إِلَى الصَّلَاةِ قَامُوا كُسَالَىٰ يُرَاءُونَ النَّاسَ وَلَا يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّـهَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا ١٤٢﴾\nAnd when they stand for prayer, they stand lazily, showing [themselves to] the people and not remembering Allah except a little.\n[An-Nisa: 142]\n3.They are confused as to which group to align with – the Muslims or the disbelievers. They are opportunists and do not know which is the more profitable side.\nمُّذَبْذَبِينَ بَيْنَ ذَٰلِكَ لَا إِلَىٰ هَٰؤُلَاءِ وَلَا إِلَىٰ هَٰؤُلَاءِ ۚ\nWavering between them, [belonging] neither to the believers nor to the disbelievers.\n[An-Nisa: 143]\n﴿وَإِذَا لَقُوا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قَالُوا آمَنَّا وَإِذَا خَلَوْا إِلَىٰ شَيَاطِينِهِمْ قَالُوا إِنَّا مَعَكُمْ إِنَّمَا نَحْنُ مُسْتَهْزِئُونَ ١٤﴾\nAnd when they meet those who believe, they say, \"We believe\"; but when they are alone with their evil ones, they say, \"Indeed, we are with you; we were only mockers.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 14]\n4.The hypocrites make the oath of Allah(swt) their armour so that their hypocrisy is hidden. But Allah(swt) has revealed an entire surah, ‘Al-Munafiqun’ describing them. It has a total of eleven verses and the translation of the first eight verses is being presented here. Please read it carefully:\n﴿إِذَا جَاءَكَ الْمُنَافِقُونَ قَالُوا نَشْهَدُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُ اللَّـهِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ يَعْلَمُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُهُ وَاللَّـهُ يَشْهَدُ إِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ لَكَاذِبُونَ ١ اتَّخَذُوا أَيْمَانَهُمْ جُنَّةً فَصَدُّوا عَن سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ ۚ إِنَّهُمْ سَاءَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ٢ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا فَطُبِعَ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ ٣ وَإِذَا رَأَيْتَهُمْ تُعْجِبُكَ أَجْسَامُهُمْ ۖ وَإِن يَقُولُوا تَسْمَعْ لِقَوْلِهِمْ ۖ كَأَنَّهُمْ خُشُبٌ مُّسَنَّدَةٌ ۖ يَحْسَبُونَ كُلَّ صَيْحَةٍ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ هُمُ الْعَدُوُّ فَاحْذَرْهُمْ ۚ قَاتَلَهُمُ اللَّـهُ ۖ أَنَّىٰ يُؤْفَكُونَ ٤ وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا يَسْتَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّـهِ لَوَّوْا رُءُوسَهُمْ وَرَأَيْتَهُمْ يَصُدُّونَ وَهُم مُّسْتَكْبِرُونَ ٥ سَوَاءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ أَسْتَغْفَرْتَ لَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ لَن يَغْفِرَ اللَّـهُ لَهُمْ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الْفَاسِقِينَ ٦ هُمُ الَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ لَا تُنفِقُوا عَلَىٰ مَنْ عِندَ رَسُولِ اللَّـهِ حَتَّىٰ يَنفَضُّوا ۗ وَلِلَّـهِ خَزَائِنُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَلَـٰكِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ لَا يَفْقَهُونَ ٧ يَقُولُونَ لَئِن رَّجَعْنَا إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ لَيُخْرِجَنَّ الْأَعَزُّ مِنْهَا الْأَذَلَّ ۚ وَلِلَّـهِ الْعِزَّةُ وَلِرَسُولِهِ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَلَـٰكِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ٨﴾\nWhen the hypocrites come to you, [O Muhammad], they say, \"We testify that you are the Messenger of Allah.\" And Allah knows that you are His Messenger, and Allah testifies that the hypocrites are liars. They have taken their oaths as a cover, so they averted [people] from the way of Allah. Indeed, it was evil that they were doing. That is because they believed, and then they disbelieved; so their hearts were sealed over, and they do not understand. And when you see them, their forms please you, and if they speak, you listen to their speech. [They are] as if they were pieces of wood propped up - they think that every shout is against them. They are the enemy, so beware of them. May Allah destroy them; how are they deluded? And when it is said to them, \"Come, the Messenger of Allah will ask forgiveness for you,\" they turn their heads aside and you see them evading while they are arrogant. It is all the same for them whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; never will Allah forgive them. Indeed, Allah does not guide the defiantly disobedient people. They are the ones who say, \"Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disband.\" And to Allah belongs the depositories of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites do not understand. They say, \"If we return to al-Madinah, the more honored [for power] will surely expel therefrom the more humble.\" And to Allah belongs [all] honor, and to His Messenger, and to the believers, but the hypocrites do not know.\n[Al-Munafiqun: 1-8]\nThis was said in front of the chieftain of the hypocrites, Abdullah-bin-Ubayy.(For more information see : Abdullah-bin-Ubayy).\nThe hypocrites are dangerous to any society and therefore their punishment will also be tough:\n﴿إِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرْكِ الْأَسْفَلِ مِنَ النَّارِ وَلَن تَجِدَ لَهُمْ نَصِيرًا ١٤٥﴾\nIndeed, the hypocrites will be in the lowest depths of the Fire - and never will you find for them a helper.\n[An-Nisa: 145]\nTraits of the hypocrites:\nThe traits of the hypocrites have been described in the sahih hadith:\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) said, \"Whoever has the following four (characteristics) will be a pure hypocrite and whoever has one of the following four characteristics will have one characteristic of hypocrisy unless and until he gives it up.\n1. Whenever he is entrusted, he betrays.\n2. Whenever he speaks, he tells a lie.\n3. Whenever he makes a covenant, he proves treacherous.\n4. Whenever he quarrels, he behaves in a very imprudent, evil and insulting manner.\"\n(Sahih Bukhari, 34 and Sahih Muslim, 58)\nThe qualities described above are called ‘Nifaq-Amal’ (Nifaq of actions). This type of nifaq can always be found. But the nifaq prevalent during the time of the Holy Prophet(saws) was ‘Nifaq-Iman’ (Nifaq of belief or faith) and it is connected with the heart and mind of a person and only Allah(swt) and His prophet(saws) were aware of it. That is why a sahabi Huzaifa(ra) said:\n“Nifaq was present during the time of Nabi(saws), but now after Iman it is only ‘kufr’”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 7114)\nThat is, nobody will be called a ‘Munafiq’ today, but there will be a ‘Momin’(believer) or a disbeliever. And if someone has any of the above mentioned four qualities, then it will be said that the person has the trait of a munafiq or hypocrite."]])